{"total":1333,"start":1,"num":100,"nextStart":101,"results":[{"id":"d257743c055e4206bd8a0f2d14af69fe","owner":"Federal_User_Community","created":1598475248000,"modified":1792177787000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities_View","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"<div><div style='text-align:center;'><span style='font-family:Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif; font-size:x-large;'>Colleges and Universities<\/span><\/div><div style='font-size:large;'>&nbsp;<\/div><\/div><div><span style='font-family:Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif; font-size:large;'>This feature layer, utilizing data from the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories. NCES uses the&nbsp;<\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:large;'>Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System&nbsp;(IPEDS)<\/span><\/a><span style='font-family:Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif; font-size:large;'>&nbsp;as the \"primary source&nbsp;for information on U.S. colleges, universities, and technical and vocational institutions.\" According to&nbsp;<\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/complete-data-files/HD2025_Dict.zip' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:large;'>NCES<\/span><\/a><span style='font-family:Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif; font-size:large;'>, this layer \"contains directory information for every institution in the 2025-26 IPEDS universe. &nbsp;Includes name, address, city, state, zip code and various URL links to the institution\"s home page, admissions, financial aid offices and &nbsp;the net price calculator. &nbsp;Identifies institutions as currently active, and institutions that participate in Title IV federal financial aid programs for which IPEDS is mandatory.<\/span><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:large;'>\"<\/span><\/div><div>&nbsp;<\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><img src='https://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/ba651221e71142d8a55a09bdbb8ae13f/data' width='800' height='400' /><br /><span style='font-size:large;'><i>University of the District of Columbia<\/i><\/span><\/div><div style='text-align:left;'><span style='font-size:large;'><strong>Data currency:<\/strong><\/span><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'>&nbsp;2025<\/span><\/div><div style='text-align:left;'><span style='font-size:large;'><strong>Data source:&nbsp;<\/strong><\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/datacenter/DataFiles.aspx?year=2025&amp;sid=18837fb2-a1a9-4ce0-bb20-e8f909f3a963&amp;rtid=7' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:large;'>IPEDS Complete Data Files<\/span><\/a><\/div><div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><strong>Data modification:<\/strong>&nbsp;None<\/span><\/div><div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-size:large;'><strong>For more information:<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:large;'>Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System<\/span><\/a><\/div><div><span style='color:#2f4f4f; font-size:large;'><font style='font-family:inherit;'><strong>Support documentation: <\/strong><\/font><\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/complete-data-files/HD2025_Dict.zip' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='color:hsl(205,58%,49%); font-size:large;'><font style='font-family:inherit;'>Data Dictionary<\/font><\/span><\/a><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='color:#2f4f4f; font-size:large;'><font style='font-family:inherit;'><strong>For feedback, please contact:<\/strong><\/font><\/span><span style='color:rgb(77,77,77); font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><font style='font-family:inherit;'>&nbsp;<\/font><\/span><a style='color:rgb(33, 117, 155); font-family:inherit; text-decoration-line:none;' href='mailto:ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com' rel='nofollow ugc'><span style='font-size:large;'><font style='font-family:inherit;'>ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com<\/font><\/span><\/a><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'>&nbsp;<\/div><\/div><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><span style='font-family:Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:x-large;'>U.S. Department of Education (ED)<\/span><br />&nbsp;<\/div><div><span style='font-size:18px;'>Per&nbsp;<\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://www.ed.gov/about' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:18px;'>ED<\/span><\/a><span style='font-size:18px;'>,&nbsp;<\/span><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(57,57,57); font-size:18px;'><span style='display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:300; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>The mission of the Department of Education (ED) is to promote student achievement and preparation for global competitiveness by fostering educational excellence and ensuring equal access for students of all ages.<\/span><\/span><\/div>","tags":["college","university","school","education","higher education","U.S. Department of Education","Department of Education","National Center for Education Statistics","NCES","IPEDS","Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System","Institute for Education Sciences","IES","degree","certificate"],"snippet":"This feature layer, utilizing data from the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), displays colleges and universities in the United States and its territories. This layer is checked annually for updates.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1791559276248.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-127.992783,23.379841],[-60.090608,51.049628]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Department of Education (ED)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<font size='4' style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif;'><img alt='Esri logo' src='https://downloads.esri.com/blogs/arcgisonline/esrilogo_new.png' style='max-width: 100%; height: auto;' /><font style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'>This work is licensed under the Esri Master License Agreement.    <\/font><\/font><p style='margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.55rem; font-size: 16px; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4'>                               <a href='https://links.esri.com/tou_summary' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>View Summary<\/a>  |  <a href='https://links.esri.com/agol_tou' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>View Terms of Use<\/a><\/font><\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_View/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":11,"numRatings":1,"avgRating":3.75,"numViews":846770,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":"livingatlas","apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"source":"Esri U.S. Federal Datasets","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"32331535785b405d869ca7a7aa3abb1f","owner":"lacounty_isd","created":1686166543000,"modified":1741648054000,"guid":null,"name":"SchoolsCollegesandUniversities","title":"Schools Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span>Current data from 2023-24 school year.  Dataset to be updated annually.<\/span><\/p><p><span style='font-weight:bold;'>Data sources:<\/span><\/p><ul><li><p><span>Public Schools (includes charter and Adult):  CDE - <\/span><a href='https://www.cde.ca.gov:443/schooldirectory/report?rid=dl1&amp;tp=txt' style='text-decoration:underline;' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>https://www.cde.ca.gov/schooldirectory/report?rid=dl1&amp;tp=txt<\/span><\/a><\/p><\/li><li><p><span>Public Schools enrollment and enhanced location:  CDE - <\/span><a href='https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=61a4260e68b14a5ab91daf27d4415e7d' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=61a4260e68b14a5ab91daf27d4415e7d<\/a><\/p><\/li><li><p><span>Private Schools type and location:  CDE - <\/span><a href='https://www.cde.ca.gov:443/schooldirectory/' style='text-decoration:underline;' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>https://www.cde.ca.gov/schooldirectory/<\/span><\/a><span>, query for <\/span><a href='https://www.cde.ca.gov/SchoolDirectory/Export?exportType=ADVS&amp;format=E&amp;tab=0&amp;reqURL=%2FSchoolDirectory%2FExportSelect%3FsimpleSearch%3DN%26address%3D%26city%3D%26counties%3D%26districts%3D%26cdscode%3D%26charter%3D%26magnet%3D%26name%3D%26nps%3D%26search%3D2%26zip%3D%26yearround%3D%26status%3D1%252C2%26types%3D%26order%3D1%26multilingual%3D%26qsc%3D3337%26qdc%3D3337%26sax%3Dtrue&amp;sax=true&amp;sd1=on&amp;sd4=on&amp;sd5=on&amp;sd6=on&amp;sd15=on&amp;sd22=on&amp;sd51=on&amp;sd52=on&amp;sd53=on&amp;sd23=on&amp;sd24=on&amp;sd25=on&amp;sd26=on' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>private schools<\/a><\/p><\/li><li><p><span>Private Schools enrollment and contact:  CDE - <\/span><a href='https://www.cde.ca.gov/ds/si/ps/documents/privateschooldata2324.xlsx' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://www.cde.ca.gov/ds/si/ps/documents/privateschooldata2324.xlsx<\/a><\/p><\/li><li><p><span>Colleges and Universities:  HIFLD - <\/span><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.hub.arcgis.com/datasets/geoplatform::colleges-and-universities/about' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://hifld-geoplatform.hub.arcgis.com/datasets/geoplatform::colleges-and-universities/about<\/a><\/p><\/li><\/ul><p><span>Public schools use location from the <\/span><a href='https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=61a4260e68b14a5ab91daf27d4415e7d' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>CDE AGOL Layer<\/a><span> where available.  This source assigns X, Y coordinates using a quality controlled geocoding and validation process to optimize positional accuracy, often geocoding to parcel.<\/span><\/p><p><span style='font-weight:bold;'>Field Descriptions:<\/span><span><\/span><\/p><ul><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Category1<\/span><span>:  Always &quot;Education&quot;<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span><span style='font-style:italic;'>Category2<\/span><span>:  School Level <\/span><span><\/span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Category3<\/span><span>:  School Type <\/span><span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Organization<\/span><span>:  School District for primary and secondary schools; data maintainer otherwise <\/span><span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Source<\/span><span>:  Source of data (see source links above) <\/span><span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Source ID<\/span><span>:  CDS Code for primary and secondary schools; IPEDS ID for colleges and universities <\/span><span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Source Date<\/span><span>:  Date listed in source <\/span><span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Enrollment<\/span><span>:  School Enrollment<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><span style='font-style:italic;'>Label Class<\/span><span>:  School classification for symbology (matches either Category2 or Category3)<\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p><i>Last Update<\/i>:  Date last updated by LA County Enterprise GIS<\/p><\/li><\/ul><p><span><\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["CDE","Education","Schools","Universities"],"snippet":"Primary and secondary schools, adult education, and colleges and universities. Includes public, charter, and private schools with enrollment where available.  2023-24 school year.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1686172457140.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-119.40376299945217,33.33111527435833],[-117.12049247581348,35.06234499784514]],"categories":["/Categories/Education"],"spatialReference":"102645","accessInformation":"California Department of Education (CDE), Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD), Los Angeles County ISD-Enterprise GIS (eGIS)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"The data herein is for informational purposes, and may not have been prepared for or be suitable for legal, engineering, or surveying intents. The County of Los Angeles reserves the right to change, restrict or discontinue access at any time. All users of the maps and data presented on https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com or deriving from any LA County REST URLs, agree to the following Terms of Use as outlined on the County of LA Enterprise GIS (eGIS) Hub (https://egis-lacounty.hub.arcgis.com/pages/terms-of-use).","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/RmCCgQtiZLDCtblq/arcgis/rest/services/Schools_Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":38400,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"RmCCgQtiZLDCtblq","scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"County of Los Angeles","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"8835ff30eaf24f299c66498958dbc018","owner":"FEMA_HQ_Preparedness_NIC","created":1755554411000,"modified":1756993034000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities","title":"Colleges and Universities RAPT","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, www.nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. This release includes the addition of 130 new records, the removal of 428 no longer reported by NCES, and modifications to the spatial location and/or attribution of 6429 records.<\/span><\/p><p><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(74,74,74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:left; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>Downloaded from HiFLD Open on July 22, 2025.<\/span><\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures Colleges and Universities defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. ","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1755559567035.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.74317458473763,-14.323171424078794],[171.3784420001386,71.32470199994994]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/XG15cJAlne2vxtgt/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":203025,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"source":"FEMA AGOL","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"207d48f54126447db20e8eb5dd172381","owner":"lahub_admin","created":1447779304000,"modified":1454547864000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"Locations of colleges and universities in Los Angeles County<div><div><br /><\/div><div>This dataset is maintained through the County of Los Angeles Location Management System. The Location Management System is used by the County of Los Angeles GIS Program to maintain a single, comprehensive geographic database of locations countywide.  For more information on the Location Management System, visit <a href='http://egis3.lacounty.gov/lms/' target='_blank'>http://egis3.lacounty.gov/lms/<\/a>.<\/div><\/div>","tags":["Los Angeles","LA","County of LA","locations","education","schools","a prosperous city"],"snippet":"Locations of colleges and universities in Los Angeles County","thumbnail":"thumbnail/County.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-118.95,32.79],[-117.64,34.82]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"4326","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p>\n<a href='http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/'>\n<img src='http://i.creativecommons.org/p/mark/1.0/88x31.png' style='border-style: none;' alt='Public Domain Mark' />\n<\/a>\n<br />\nThis work is free of known copyright restrictions.\n<\/p>","culture":"english (united states)","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"http://public.gis.lacounty.gov/public/rest/services/LACounty_Dynamic/LMS_Data_Public/MapServer/45","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":213523,"scoreCompleteness":95,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792389600000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"b31dc406c3df451ea3d5299cf698b265","owner":"CA_Office_of_Emergency_Services_GIS","created":1516143076000,"modified":1556239680000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<font size='4'><span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);'>The <\/span><a href='https://calema.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=b31dc406c3df451ea3d5299cf698b265' target='_blank'>Colleges and Universities<\/a><span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);'> feature class is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, <\/span><a href='http://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/)' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif !important;' target='_blank'><font color='#098ea6'>http://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/)<\/font><\/a><span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);'>, National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/). Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories.<\/span><\/font>","tags":["ESF6","ESF6 Care and Shelter","Care and Shelter","Education","College","University","People and Place","Management","ESF5","ESF5 Management","Government","Data Library","Basedata","CalOES Data Library"],"snippet":"The Colleges and Universities feature class is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/b31dc406c3df451ea3d5299cf698b265.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-126.451,32.393],[-113.443,42.548]],"categories":["/Categories/Cal OES Operational Products/Owned By/CalOES Data Library - Basedata","/Categories/Emergency Support Functions/ESF5 Management","/Categories/Cal OES Operational Products/Authoritative Data Source/U.S. Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD)","/Categories/Cal OES Operational Products/Infrastructure/Education","/Categories/Done","/Categories/Emergency Support Functions/ESF6 Care and Shelter"],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL) Geographic Information Science and Technology (GIST) Group, National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;'><font size='4'>Public Use<\/font><\/span><\/p>\n\n<span style='line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4'>This product is for\nuse by Cal OES personnel and supporting partners to conduct emergency\nmanagement operations. The information contained herein has been compiled from\nvarious local, state, and federal agencies. This information is constantly\nchanging, and Cal OES does not verify or certify the information contained\nherein<\/font><\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/Hp6G80Pky0om7QvQ/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":150474,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792371600000,"source":"CA Governor's Office of Emergency Services","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"ce5bbbe0c8194778859df0d3e02be3e7","owner":"nconemap","created":1484248454000,"modified":1679499870000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>The Colleges and Universities dataset is composed of any type of Post Secondary Education such as: colleges, universities, technical schools, trade schools, business schools, satellite (branch) campuses, etc. that grant First Professional, Associate, Bachelors, Masters, or Doctoral degrees.    Text fields in this dataset have been set to all upper case to facilitate consistent database engine search results.    All diacritics (e.g. the German umlaut or the Spanish tilde) have been replaced with their closest equivalent English character to facilitate use with database systems that may not support diacritics.    The currentness of this dataset is indicated by the [CONTDATE] attribute. Based upon this attribute, the oldest record dates from 07/09/2007 and the newest record dates from 07/26/2007.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["Universities and colleges","Community colleges","Junior colleges","Cooking schools","Business schools","Medical colleges","Trade schools","Law schools","Dental schools","Military education","Sports camps","Conservatories of music","Art Study and teaching","Massage therapy","Aviation technician training course.","Theological seminaries","Executives Training of","Bible colleges","Technical institutes","Church and college","Health occupations schools","Islamic universities and colleges","Private universities and colleges","Public universities and colleges","Universities and colleges Religion","structure","NC","North Carolina","Department of Information Technology","DIT","Center for Geographic Information and Analysis","CGIA","NC OneMap"],"snippet":"Homeland Security\n\nUse Cases: Use cases help define and clarify requirements, and describe how the data may be used.\n\n1) Identification of populations that may need to be evacuated in the event of an emergency.\n\n2) Notification of groups of people who may be at risk from a contagious disease outbreak.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-84.0442,33.9402],[-76.1891,36.4512]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":"https://www.nconemap.gov/pages/terms","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.nconemap.gov/secure/rest/services/NC1Map_Education/MapServer/0","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":41329,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792389600000,"source":"Techni Graphic Systems, Inc.","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"7fb7ebf5fa234fdab46da3f94a813ecd","owner":"NJDCA.GIS","created":1747925670000,"modified":1748015015000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_And_Universities","title":"Colleges And Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>This dataset contains the campus boundaries of Colleges and Universities of New Jersey mapped by parcel boundaries.<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN><SPAN>The Colleges and Universities dataset is composed of any type of Post Secondary Education such as: colleges, universities, technical schools, trade schools, business schools, satellite (branch) campuses, etc. that grant First Professional, Associate, Bachelors, Masters, or Doctoral degrees. Secondary education facilities, Administrative offices, or Post Secondary Education facilities that are non degree granting schools are intended to be excluded from this dataset, but a few may be included. All data is non license restricted data that has been added from TGS research. <\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>May 2025:<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>Updated list with new Colleges and Universities, additional branch campuses, name changes, and closures. based on the <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://www.nj.gov/highereducation/colleges/schools_sector.shtml\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>OSHE list of accredited institutions<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/A><SPAN>. A parcel based approach was employed to accurately reflect changes in campus boundaries. <\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN /><\/P><P><SPAN /><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["Colleges and Universities","College","University"],"snippet":"The College and University file was created to help implement the NJ State Development and Redevelopment Plan by helping to identify areas where technology/health related activities and businesses could locate. Updated May 2025 by NJ Department of Community Affairs for use in the Community Asset Map and other web applications.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-75.594236,38.893698],[-73.822727,41.433]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102711","accessInformation":"New Jersey Office for Planning Advocacy, NJ Office of GIS, TGS Research, New Jersey Department of Community Affairs (NJDCA) Local Planning Services (LPS).","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p>This data set is not survey data and must not be used as survey data. See the balance of this metadata record for conditions that limit appropriate uses. Acknowledgement of the data set providers [NJ Department of Community Affairs (NJDCA) Office of Local Planning Services (LPS); and NJ Office of Information Technology, Office of GIS (NJOGIS)], would be appreciated for maps, data or other products derived from this data set. The State of New Jersey makes great effort to provide secure, accurate, and complete data and metadata. However, portions of the data and metadata may be incorrect or not current. Any errors or omissions should be reported for investigation. The State of New Jersey, its officers, employees or agents shall not be liable for damages or losses of any kind arising out of or in connection with the use or performance of data and metadata, including but not limited to, damages or losses caused by reliance upon the accuracy or timeliness of any such data and metadata, or damages incurred from the viewing, distributing, or copying of those materials. The data and metadata are provided \"as is.\" No warranty of any kind, implied, expressed, or statutory, including but not limited to the warranties of non-infringement of third party rights, title, merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and freedom from computer virus, is given with respect to the data and metadata, or its hyperlinks to other Internet resources. The State disclaims any duty or obligation either to maintain availability of or to update the data and metadata. All web site data distribution by the Department of Community Affairs is, in addition, subject to the Conditions of Use for State of New Jersey executive branch web sites, listed on the<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.nj.gov/nj/legal.html\">State\u2019s Legal Statement Disclaimers page.<\/a><\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/Aur8tCo478N3VovT/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_And_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":27408,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792389600000,"source":"New Jersey Department of State, Office for Planning Advocacy","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"f4f9db61af1d4392b5985dc7a160bd8b","owner":"grs_asu","created":1715819530000,"modified":1715819556000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges_and_Universities_Campuses","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges point feature classes/shapefiles with a POPULATION value greater than or equal to 500. Also included is a subset of campuses with a POPULATION value under 500 or equal to -999. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Excluded are online institutions and administrative records as well as colleges and universities that do not have a verifiable campus map. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class/shapefile contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges and Colleges and Universities. Note that attribution is derived from the Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges feature classes/shapefiles. Refer to the metadata of those feature classes/shapefiles for further information regarding attribution. This release includes 21 new records and the removal of 88 records that are no longer applicable based on the sourced datasets.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","boundary","campus","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures College and University Campuses defined by the Colleges and Universities point feature class/shapefile and Supplemental Colleges point feature class/shapefile for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.74437785899997,-14.323952233999938],[171.37880784200001,66.90102666300004]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services3.arcgis.com/0OPQIK59PJJqLK0A/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_Campuses/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":4199,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"Arizona State University","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"4a84ec5d58a345f5b4ea0ef494819df1","owner":"StarkCountyOH","created":1421075474000,"modified":1784300779000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"<font size='4'>This layer serves as an inventory of colleges and universities within Stark County, Ohio. <\/font><span style='font-size: large;'>It is part of the Stark County Community Features umbrella of layers, which includes <\/span><a href='https://scgisa.starkcountyohio.gov/arcgis/rest/services/RegionalPlanningCommission/CommunityFeatures/MapServer' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>CommunityFeatures<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://scgisa.starkcountyohio.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Auditor/LiveWorkLocate/MapServer' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>LiveWorkLocate<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, and <\/span><a href='https://scgisa.starkcountyohio.gov/arcgis/rest/services/EmergencyResponse/EmergencyResponseFacilities/MapServer' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>EmergencyResponseFacilities<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>. These layers depict places of interest throughout the county, including <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=898018b17a4241918c2dad958b8e8566' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Airfields and Helipads<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><font size='4'>Colleges and Universities<\/font><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=bc3f0717be9140268e73206f435733c1' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Corporate Headquarters<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=9f928fbc669147d382395fde634fa7ca' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>EMS Facilities<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><font size='4'><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=ce4a8d53bc084a82adb3ed7972b479b6' target='_blank'>Event Venues<\/a>, <\/font><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=1ac59457de5b4743a2eb3a57a4763172' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Fire Stations<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=c263d1317fa94a06a94dca6d51c9eec3' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Golf Courses<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=5abcc257d6734f1e8b3d8717cd049bb6' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Hospitals and Health Clinics<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=123248287d22454ba97ec8d2252e4c69' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Museums and Historic Landmarks<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=ddf64feaedfb4443a92afc7172bd7ae7' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Parks and Recreation Areas<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=42698b87fb2e46e3afd9ea1c8180a13f' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Places of Worship<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=1e2e8edd2fff4f4fb64f7e0a7854fe11' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Police Stations<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=9a946731447444908d99286102c59985#overview' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Post Offices<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=173b3e8ce9134d9784640671b7894be3' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Public Libraries<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=a96b1b734b9d4f29aafbc8c1bf706d50' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Retail Centers<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=48a34310312440c29745d00e788b17aa' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Schools and Daycares<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>, and <\/span><a href='https://starkcountyohio.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=f8bc057741bb4433afc603cbdedc10e3' style='font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Senior Citizen Centers<\/a><span style='font-size: large;'>. These &quot;community features&quot; were first inventoried and digitized by the Stark County Regional Planning Commission (RPC) in 2008. The initial inventory was a collaborative effort between RPC and each community within the county, who provided lists of their respective features. Since then, each layer is periodically updated by RPC and Stark County GIS.<\/span>","tags":["Colleges","Stark County","Ohio","Universities","SCGIS","Education","Community Features","LiveWorkLocate","Meeting Facilities"],"snippet":"Colleges and universities within Stark County, Ohio. Part of the Community Features umbrella of layers.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1558717745673.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-81.4931,40.7606],[-81.1058,40.9107]],"categories":["/Categories/County/GIS/Open Data","/Categories/County/GIS/General"],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Stark County GIS (SCGIS), Stark County Regional Planning Commission (SCRPC), ajkarapandzich","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-size: small;'>Public information data furnished by Stark County must be accepted and used by the recipient with the understanding that Stark County makes no warranties, expressed or implied, concerning the accuracy, completeness, reliability, or suitability of this data. This product may not be suitable for legal, engineering, or surveying purposes and its boundaries are for reference only. Furthermore, Stark County assumes no liability, whatsoever, associated with the use or misuse of such data.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://scgisa.starkcountyohio.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Auditor/LiveWorkLocate/MapServer/2","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":21650,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792317600000,"source":"Stark County Ohio"},{"id":"4f3d1f60ab4d4333a21c487024d69699","owner":"bcgisdata_BCGIS","created":1536951982000,"modified":1785848661000,"guid":null,"name":"OpenDataCollegesAndUniversities","title":"Broward County Colleges And Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<b>Overview<\/b><p>This feature service provides location-based records for colleges and universities in Broward County, Florida. It supports browser-based and GIS workflows that need a maintained inventory of higher education facilities and their associated site information.<\/p><b>Feature Layer<\/b><p>The <strong>CollegesAndUniversities<\/strong> layer contains point features representing higher education facilities. The layer includes facility identification and status details, along with location and address information used to support search, display, and reference in local planning and infrastructure applications.<\/p><b>Geographic Coverage<\/b><p>The service covers Broward County, Florida, within the area supported by the referenced infrastructure dataset.<\/p><b>Use Cases<\/b><ul><li>Inventorying colleges and universities for local government and planning workflows<\/li><li>Supporting campus location lookup and map display<\/li><li>Integrating higher education facilities into county infrastructure and public information applications<\/li><li>Providing reference data for education-related spatial analysis and asset management<\/li><\/ul><b>Source and Attribution<\/b><p>Data credits include FPL, BCGIS, and BCEMD. The service is published under Broward Terms of Use.<\/p>","tags":["Broward County","Florida","colleges","universities","higher education","education facilities","campus locations","public institutions","Broward","Broward County Florida","Broward County GIS","Broward Sites","Local Database Broward County","GIS","BCGIS","BC GIS","geographic","geographical","geographic analysis","geographies","local geography","county-level geography","Board of County Commissioners"],"snippet":"Location records for colleges and universities in Broward County, Florida, with facility and address details for GIS and public information use.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-80.40418195657692,25.981872066574866],[-80.09663072221952,26.32148314171764]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"NAD_1983_HARN_StatePlane_Florida_East_FIPS_0901_Feet","accessInformation":"FPL, BCGIS, BCEMD","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;font-size:12pt\"><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 11 0;\"><SPAN><SPAN>Broward Terms of Use - http://www.broward.org/Terms/Pages/Default.aspx <\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/JMAJrTsHNLrSsWf5/arcgis/rest/services/OpenDataCollegesAndUniversities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":3755,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"             Broward County GIS"},{"id":"6aea00cdaeac4cfdad24c8e23f9ae052","owner":"planning_cra","created":1738197909000,"modified":1742839892000,"guid":null,"name":"College_and_University_Campuses_in_Coachella_Valley","title":"College and University Campuses in Coachella Valley","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges point feature classes/shapefiles with a POPULATION value greater than or equal to 500. Also included is a subset of campuses with a POPULATION value under 500 or equal to -999. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Excluded are online institutions and administrative records as well as colleges and universities that do not have a verifiable campus map. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class/shapefile contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges and Colleges and Universities. Note that attribution is derived from the Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges feature classes/shapefiles. Refer to the metadata of those feature classes/shapefiles for further information regarding attribution. This release includes 21 new records and the removal of 88 records that are no longer applicable based on the sourced datasets.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","boundary","campus","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures College and University Campuses defined by the Colleges and Universities point feature class/shapefile and Supplemental Colleges point feature class/shapefile for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-116.972853756812,33.70181429567817],[-116.21878933816909,33.91967733046117]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services8.arcgis.com/WunV6yKxvEXfsV4W/arcgis/rest/services/College_and_University_Campuses_in_Coachella_Valley/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2974,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"40fd8cd3fcd34c31915cda47a1a8cb0f","owner":"planning_cra","created":1738198635000,"modified":1742839859000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities_in_Coachella_Valley","title":"Colleges and Universities in Coachella Valley","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, http://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. This release includes the addition of 130 new records, the removal of 428 no longer reported by NCES, and modifications to the spatial location and/or attribution of 6429 records.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures Colleges and Universities defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://gii.dhs.gov/HIFLD)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-117.00166370502549,33.690013186589034],[-116.18568226702095,33.953405982566196]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services8.arcgis.com/WunV6yKxvEXfsV4W/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_in_Coachella_Valley/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2899,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"607ecde42f634f70ac56a61342de0870","owner":"sara.hedrick@indianaffairs.gov_BIA_Geospatial","created":1687809025000,"modified":1755627763000,"guid":null,"name":"TCU_Colleges","title":"Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCU)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p>Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs) are chartered by their respective tribal governments, including the ten tribes within the largest reservations in the United States. The 33 accredited TCUs operate more than 90 campuses and sites in 15 states\u2014covering most of Indian Country\u2014and serve students from well more than 250 federally recognized Indian tribes. TCUs vary in enrollment (size), focus (liberal arts, sciences, workforce development/training), location (woodlands, desert, frozen tundra, rural, urban), and student population (predominantly American Indian). However, tribal identity is the core of every TCU, and they all share the mission of tribal self-determination and service to their respective communities.<\/p><p>These academically rigorous institutions engage in partnerships with organizations including U.S. Department of the Interior, U.S. Department of Agriculture, U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, the National Science Foundation, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, and universities nationwide to support research and education programs that focus on issues such as climate change, sustainable agriculture, water quality, wildlife population dynamics, and diabetes prevention. Many support distance learning involving state-of-the-art learning environments.<\/p>","tags":["BOGS","Pathways"],"snippet":"Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs) are a category of Minority Serving Institutions in the United States higher education system. They are distinguished as tribal schools because they are chartered by tribal governments and are located on or near American Indian reservations.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1755626034100.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-156.68029785199997,31.990072250000026],[-84.60644531299994,71.32501220700004]],"categories":["/Categories/Education"],"spatialReference":"4326","accessInformation":"Bureau of Indian Affairs, Branch of Geospatial Support (BOGS), BIA Pathways Program, Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database.","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div>No warranty is made by the Bureau of Indian Affairs (BIA) for the use of the data for purposes not intended by the BIA. This GIS Dataset may contain errors. There is no impact on the legal status of the land areas depicted herein and no impact on land ownership. No legal inference can or should be made from the information in this GIS Dataset. The GIS Dataset is prepared strictly for illustrative and reference purposes only and should not be used, and is not intended for legal, survey, engineering or navigation purposes. <\/div><div><br /><\/div><div>These data have been developed from the best available sources. Although efforts have been made to ensure that the data are accurate and reliable, errors and variable conditions originating from source documents and/or the translation of information from source documents to the systems of record continue to exist. Users must be aware of these conditions and bear responsibility for the appropriate use of the information with respect to possible errors, scale, resolution, rectification, positional accuracy, development methodology, time period, environmental and climatic conditions and other circumstances specific to these data. The user is responsible for understanding the accuracy limitations of the data provided herein. The burden for determining fitness for use lies entirely with the user. The user should refer to the accompanying metadata notes for a description of the data and data development procedures. <\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/UxqqIfhng71wUT9x/arcgis/rest/services/TCU_Colleges/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":18534,"scoreCompleteness":91,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"Bureau of Indian Affairs","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"112f9bbbcfe643b89929b05c22fd682e","owner":"FX.AuthData","created":1783520412000,"modified":1791819664000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"The locations of the colleges and universities within Fairfax County.Contact: Fairfax County Department of Information Technology GIS DivisionData Accessibility: Publicly availableUpdate frequency: As NeededLast Revision Date: 1/1/2000Creation Date: 1/1/2000Feature Dataset name: GISMGR.POINTS_OF_INTERESTLayer name: GISMGR.COLLEGES_UNIVERSITIES","tags":["FFX","Fairfax County","Virginia","VA","Fairfax County Department of Information Technology GIS Division","Colleges & Universities","Fairfax County","Virginia","VA","schools","Open Data","FFX-Education"],"snippet":"This layer contains the locations of the colleges and universities within Fairfax County. For use as points of interest for display and analysis.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1791819663352.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-77.30703277626182,38.82990625195534],[-77.23601162724381,38.83446672491995]],"categories":["/Categories/Community/Public Facilities"],"spatialReference":"102746","accessInformation":"Fairfax County GIS Division, Virginia, Department of Information Technology","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><a href='https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/maps/disclaimer' style='text-decoration:underline;' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/maps/disclaimer<\/span><\/a><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/ioennV6PpG5Xodq0/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1755,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"ioennV6PpG5Xodq0","scoreCompleteness":95,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"County of Fairfax","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"a6c837ea38f94d7380d1ba37b83d5c76","owner":"Wisconsin_DPI","created":1620226094000,"modified":1686328149000,"guid":null,"name":"WI_Colleges_and_Universities_2021","title":"Colleges and Universities, Wisconsin, 2021","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>This dataset contains geocoded locations of higher education institutions located in Wisconsin. Information exported from <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://nces.ed.gov:443/collegenavigator/\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) College Navigator<\/SPAN><\/A><SPAN>. <\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["higher education","universities","NCES","colleges","Wisconsin","Wisconsin Department of Public Instruction"],"snippet":"Locations of higher education institutions in Wisconsin.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1627508967058.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-92.82009118092199,42.46899397941548],[-87.52330746802865,46.749592429236195]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"3071","accessInformation":"Wisconsin Department of Public Instruction","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><p>The Department of Public Instruction (DPI) has made a reasonable effort to ensure that the accompanying information is up-to-date, accurate, complete, and comprehensive at the time of disclosure. <span>The layer is intended for your reference use only. It contains the best information the Department of Public Instruction (DPI) has to date, but no guarantee of accuracy is made. It should not be used for any land transactions, financial decisions, taxation, surveying, or other similar uses. <\/span><\/p><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services8.arcgis.com/o4NJgD3NfeHnWy06/arcgis/rest/services/WI_Colleges_and_Universities_2021/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":10831,"scoreCompleteness":90,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"source":"Wisconsin Department of Public Instruction","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"991be1af3dc745ed92ba276f3fcb3915","owner":"TVictoria_westcovina","created":1620771417000,"modified":1712875973000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>Data was extracted from ESRI Living Atlas and clipped to show colleges and universities within West Covina.<\/span><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><br /><\/span><\/div><div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><br /><\/span><\/div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), US Department of Education for the 2018-2019 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. <\/span><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the &quot;Place Keyword&quot; section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. <\/span>","tags":["Education","University","College","Health and Human Services"],"snippet":"Colleges or Universities within West Covina","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-117.94962717340584,34.069392687343424],[-117.89759272320558,34.076781392821985]],"categories":["/Categories/Health and Human Services"],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"ESRI Living Atlas; The City of West Covina, GIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:small;'>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the data set's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services8.arcgis.com/WV8ogNubjFL2BKPt/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1571,"scoreCompleteness":93,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792371600000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"de1464fec6d64b9591e109cfab6a3f38","owner":"topsoil.integration_detroitmi","created":1721752106000,"modified":1778182547000,"guid":null,"name":"Detroit_Colleges_and_Universities","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p>The schools, districts, and other educational institutions in the Detroit Educational Institutions datasets were identified from the <a href='https://cepi.state.mi.us/eem/' rel='nofollow ugc'>State of Michigan Center for Educational Performance and Information (CEPI)<\/a> Educational Entity Master (EEM) database. Schools of all statuses (Open - Active; Open - Pending; Open - Inactive; Open - Under construction/remodeling; Open - Vacant/empty; Closed \u2013 Pending; Closed) are included in the dataset to provide access to information about schools that currently and previously operated in Detroit. Educational institutions with a mailing address in Detroit but a physical location outside the City are not included in this dataset. Each record in the dataset represents an educational entity, which may be a school, a district, or other entity directly associated with an educational institution. The word, \"entity\" is used in field (i.e., column) names and descriptions when a field is applicable to multiple types units associated with an educational entity (e.g., if applicable to schools, districts, and other facilities).<\/p>\n<p>Link to metadata: https://cepi.state.mi.us/eem/Documents/ColumnDescriptions.pdf<\/p>","tags":["Mart","Public","odp","education","schools"],"snippet":"Colleges and universities with a physical location in the City of Detroit that have a record in the State of Michigan Center for Educational Performance and Information (CEPI) Educational Entity Master (EEM) database.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1742909754534.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-83.1698543274516,42.3271596450254],[-83.0542532150134,42.41980380100006]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"4326","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/qvkbeam7Wirps6zC/arcgis/rest/services/Detroit_Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":9298,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"source":"City of Detroit"},{"id":"ded9eed1d9ba45d09ba50644bd44060d","owner":"walkerc1","created":1707855275000,"modified":1773850164000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges point feature classes/shapefiles with a POPULATION value greater than or equal to 500. Also included is a subset of campuses with a POPULATION value under 500 or equal to -999. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Excluded are online institutions and administrative records as well as colleges and universities that do not have a verifiable campus map. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class/shapefile contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges and Colleges and Universities. Note that attribution is derived from the Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges feature classes/shapefiles. Refer to the metadata of those feature classes/shapefiles for further information regarding attribution. This release includes 21 new records and the removal of 88 records that are no longer applicable based on the sourced datasets.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","boundary","campus","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures College and University Campuses defined by the Colleges and Universities point feature class/shapefile and Supplemental Colleges point feature class/shapefile for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-80.68994420914792,26.36505477009002],[-80.07699999233765,26.889499655151553]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services9.arcgis.com/wo4TbGW3178yjJ8x/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1118,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"14da560d7c224572bf9fea522f6b857f","owner":"IndianaMap","created":1780335503000,"modified":1780335504000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities_2020","title":"Colleges and Universities 2020","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["providerSDS","Feature Access","Feature Service","ArcGIS Server","Metadata","Service","Data"],"description":"The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the &quot;Place Keyword&quot; section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. This release includes the addition of 130 new records, the removal of 428 no longer reported by NCES, and modifications to the spatial location and/or attribution of 6429 records.","tags":["Education","College","University","Post Secondary"],"snippet":"This dataset captures Colleges and Universities defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. https://gis.dhs.gov/HIFLD. Data for Indiana was downloaded from the HIFLD open geospatial portal on 5/1/2023 (https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/geoplatform::colleges-and-universities/about)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1682948111297.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-87.67779024399994,37.96424873900003],[-84.82571299999995,41.717835208000054]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"4326","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>LIMITATION OF WARRANTIES AND LIABILITY - This product is provided &quot;AS IS&quot;, without any other warranties or conditions, expressed or implied, including, but not limited to, warranties for product quality, or suitability to a particular purpose or use. The risk or liability resulting from the use of this product is assumed by the user. The Indiana Geographic Information Office shares no liability with product users indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages whatsoever, including, but not limited to, loss of revenue or profit, lost or damaged data or other commercial or economic loss. The Indiana Geographic Information Office is not responsible for claims by a third party.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://gisdata.in.gov/server/rest/services/Hosted/Colleges_and_Universities_2020/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":"","banner":"","screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":948,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792389600000,"source":"IndianaMap","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"43246c8cc22145ef8b4a2d9851be3a24","owner":"afitz_jsapi","created":1621631643000,"modified":1621869743000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:large;'>This feature layer, utilizing data from the U.S. Department of Education (USDED), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories. The feature layer is composed of all post secondary education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) and the USDED. Included are doctoral/research universities, masters colleges and universities, baccalaureate colleges, associates colleges, theological seminaries, medical schools and other health care professions. Also included in the data are schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, law schools, teachers colleges, tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions.<\/span><br /><\/div><div><br /><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><img alt='USDED Colleges and Universities - screen capture and popup - 800x400' src='https://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/6fe8e47884df42d3919c4aabd9a9f3f6/data' /><br /><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><font size='4'><i>Gallaudet University<\/i><\/font><\/div><div style='text-align:left;'><font size='4' style='font-family: inherit;'>Data currency: see <\/font><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities' rel='nofollow ugc' target='_blank'><font size='4'>Colleges and Universities<\/font><\/a><br /><\/div><div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><font size='4'>Data downloaded from: <\/font><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) &gt; <\/font><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities' rel='nofollow ugc' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Colleges and Universities<\/font><\/a><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-size:large;'>Data modification(s): none<\/span><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-size:large;'>For more information: <\/span><a href='https://www.ed.gov/' rel='nofollow ugc' style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large; color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank'>USDED<\/a><span style='font-size:large;'>; <\/span><a href='https://nces.ed.gov/' rel='nofollow ugc' style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large; color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank'>NCES<\/a><span style='font-size:large;'>; <\/span><a href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' rel='nofollow ugc' style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large; color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank'>IPEDS<\/a><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><font color='#000000' style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/font><\/font><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><font color='#000000' style='font-family:inherit;'>For feedback please contact:<\/font><span style='font-family:inherit; color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'> <\/span><a href='mailto:ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com' rel='nofollow ugc' style='color:rgb(33, 117, 155); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;'>ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com<\/a><br /><\/font><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/font><\/div><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><i>Thumbnail image courtesy of: <\/i><i><a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/' rel='nofollow ugc' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank'>Antonio Barrera<\/a><\/i><\/font><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><i><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Symbol source image courtesy of <a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/us/' rel='nofollow ugc' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank'>Hector<\/a><\/font><\/i><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:17px;'><span style='font-family:Arial, sans-serif; color:black; font-size:15pt;'><br /><\/span><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:17px;'><span style='font-family:Arial, sans-serif; color:black; font-size:15pt;'>Other Federal User Community federally focused content that may interest you:<\/span><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='font-family:inherit; color:rgb(68, 68, 68);'><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.55rem;'><\/p><ul><li><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir LT W01 35 Light&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color:rgb(76, 76, 76);'> <\/span><\/font><a href='http://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/apps/MinimalGallery/index.html?appid=ad0f78f184f24bb9b80ec02b41d0fb3a' rel='nofollow ugc' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit; font-size:17px;' target='_blank'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Department of Education<\/font><\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["U.S. Department of Education","Department of Education","USDED","college","university","education","higher learning","school","Post Secondary","specialized institutions","Integrated Post Secondary Education System","National Center for Education Statistics","IPEDS","NCES","places","federal"],"snippet":"This feature layer, utilizing data from the U.S. Department of Education, displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7432,-14.3232],[171.3785,71.3247]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"U.S. Department of Education (USDED)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<font size='4' style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif;'><img alt='Esri logo' src='https://downloads.esri.com/blogs/arcgisonline/esrilogo_new.png' style='max-width: 100%; height: auto;' /><font style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'>This work is licensed under the Esri Master License Agreement.    <\/font><\/font><p style='margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.55rem; font-size: 16px; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4'>                               <a href='https://links.esri.com/tou_summary' rel='nofollow ugc' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none;' target='_blank'>View Summary<\/a>  |  <a href='https://links.esri.com/agol_tou' rel='nofollow ugc' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;' target='_blank'>View Terms of Use<\/a><\/font><\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_View/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":5106,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792375200000,"source":"Esri JSAPI","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"f372a03ee177491bb57057eb79a48c69","owner":"BucknellGIS","created":1681394991000,"modified":1681394992000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities in the United States-Copy","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div><font face='Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif'><div style='text-align:center;'><font size='5'>Colleges and Universities in the United States<\/font><\/div><div style='font-size:large;'><br /><\/div><\/font><\/div><div><font face='Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif' size='4'>This feature layer, utilizing data from Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories. According to <\/font><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/geoplatform::colleges-and-universities/about' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><font size='4'>HIFLD<\/font><\/a><font face='Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif' size='4'>, this feature layer &quot;is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions.&quot;<\/font><br /><\/div><div><br /><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><img alt='USDED Colleges and Universities - screen capture and popup - 800x400' src='https://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/a60cfe41aa924da292ce5d49cfc733db/data' /><br /><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><font size='4'><i>Washington and Lee University &amp; Virginia Military Institute<\/i><\/font><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><font size='4'><i><br /><\/i><\/font><\/div><div style='text-align:left;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><b>Data currency:<\/b> <\/font><font size='4'>This cached Esri service is checked monthly for updates from its source (<\/font><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><font size='4'>Colleges and Universities<\/font><\/a><font size='4'>).<\/font><\/div><div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='font-size:large; font-family:inherit;'><b>Data modification:<\/b> none<\/span><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><div style='font-family:inherit;'><b><font size='4'>For more information:<\/font><\/b><font size='4'> <a href='https://www.ed.gov/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>U.S. Department of Education<\/a>; <a href='https://nces.ed.gov/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>National Center for Education Statistics<\/a>; <a href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System<\/a><\/font><font size='4' style='font-size:16px; font-family:inherit;'><font color='#000000' style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/font><\/font><\/div><div style='font-size:16px; font-family:inherit;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><font color='#2f4f4f' style='font-family:inherit;'><b>For feedback, please contact:<\/b><\/font><span style='font-family:inherit; color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'> <\/span><a href='mailto:ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com' style='color:rgb(33, 117, 155); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' rel='nofollow ugc'>ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com<\/a><br /><\/font><\/div><div style='font-size:16px; font-family:inherit;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/font><\/div><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><i>Thumbnail image courtesy of: <\/i><i><a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Antonio Barrera<\/a><\/i><\/font><\/div><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/font><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><font face='Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif' size='5'>Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD)<\/font><br /><\/div><div style='text-align:center;'><font size='4'><font face='Avenir Next W01, Avenir Next W00, Avenir Next, Avenir, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'><br /><\/font><\/font><\/div><div><font size='4'>Per <\/font><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.hub.arcgis.com/' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><font size='4'>HIFLD<\/font><\/a><font size='4'>, &quot;The Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Subcommittee was established\u2026to address improvements in collection, processing, sharing, and protection of homeland infrastructure geospatial information across multiple levels of government, and to develop a common foundation of homeland infrastructure data to be used for visualization and analysis on all classification domains.&quot;<br /><\/font><\/div>","tags":["U.S. Department of Education","Department of Education","USDED","college","university","education","higher learning","school","Post Secondary","specialized institutions","Integrated Post Secondary Education System","National Center for Education Statistics","IPEDS","NCES","places","federal"],"snippet":"This feature layer, utilizing data from Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7432,-14.3232],[171.3784,71.3247]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"U.S. Department of Education (USDED); Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<font size='4' style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif;'><img alt='Esri logo' src='https://downloads.esri.com/blogs/arcgisonline/esrilogo_new.png' style='max-width: 100%; height: auto;' /><font style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'>This work is licensed under the Esri Master License Agreement.    <\/font><\/font><p style='margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.55rem; font-size: 16px; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4'>                               <a href='https://links.esri.com/tou_summary' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>View Summary<\/a>  |  <a href='https://links.esri.com/agol_tou' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>View Terms of Use<\/a><\/font><\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_View/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":4533,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792378800000,"source":"Bucknell GIS & Spatial Thinking","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"1343ade5e7294c43b8ff9cbdfb2d721d","owner":"MassEOEEA","created":1676994086000,"modified":1779737665000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Massachusetts Colleges and Universities    Source: MassGIS","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left; font-size:12pt;'><p><span>The locations of institutions of higher education in Massachusetts. Sites appearing in this layer are those normally attended by students after completion of high school. Types are public and private, and categories include co-ed, vocational, technical, religious, medical, and traditional 2- and 4-year colleges and universities.<\/span><\/p><p>See the <a href='https://www.mass.gov/info-details/massgis-data-colleges-and-universities' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>MassGIS metadata page<\/a> (<a href='https://www.mass.gov/info-details/massgis-data-colleges-and-universities' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://www.mass.gov/info-details/massgis-data-colleges-and-universities<\/a>) for more information about this datalayer.<\/p><\/div>","tags":["Colleges","Universities","Higher Education","Technical","Vocational","Professional","Certificate","Schools","MassGIS","Massachusetts"],"snippet":"Colleges and universities in Massachusetts  Source: MassGIS","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1676994447305.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-73.3974,41.2903],[-70.0058,42.7974]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"26986","accessInformation":"MassGIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/hGdibHYSPO59RG1h/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer/0","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":4781,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"7iJyYTjCtKsZS1LR","scoreCompleteness":78,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"MA Executive Office of Energy and Environmental Affairs"},{"id":"0ecf50bd3a2f49a8a30599193e661c86","owner":"kwinchester_sts","created":1773778372000,"modified":1787934551000,"guid":null,"name":"College_University_view","title":"College and University view","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service","View Service"],"description":"<p><strong>Overview<\/strong><\/p><p>This Feature Service provides detailed geographic information on colleges and universities located within the state of Tennessee. It encompasses a single feature layer that maps educational institutions with their corresponding geographic coordinates and associated attributes.<\/p><p><strong>Feature Layer<\/strong><\/p><ul><li><strong>College University:<\/strong> This layer contains point features representing colleges and universities. Attributes include the institution's name, location name, county, full address, city, state, zip code, latitude, longitude, and FIPS code. The data facilitates spatial analysis related to higher education facilities across Tennessee.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Geographic Coverage<\/strong><\/p><p>The dataset covers educational institutions across multiple counties within the state of Tennessee, offering insight into their distribution throughout the region.<\/p><p><strong>Use Cases<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Planning and analysis for educational service delivery and accessibility.<\/li><li>Mapping and visualization of college and university locations for academic and administrative purposes.<\/li><li>Supporting research and development projects related to higher education infrastructure and demographics.<\/li><\/ul>","tags":["Tennessee","colleges","universities","higher education","educational institutions"],"snippet":"Map of colleges and universities across Tennessee providing locations and related address information for educational planning and analysis.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1773778535884.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-90.03910698499999,35.04582187900007],[-82.15341448899994,36.58717868700006]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"4326","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p><span style='color:rgb(5,5,5); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;; font-size:10px;'>The State of Tennessee makes no representation or warranty as to the accuracy of this map and the information contained within nor to its fitness for a particular purpose or use. The user accepts this map on an \u201cAS IS\u201d basis and assumes all responsibilities for the use thereof. The user will assume the entire risk and agrees to hold the State of Tennessee and its staff harmless of any liability resulting from any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or other damages, including loss of profit, arising out of the use of this map. The user is responsible for independent verification of all information contained on this map.<\/span><\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/YuVBSS7Y1of2Qud1/arcgis/rest/services/College_University_view/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":425,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"State of Tennessee STS GIS","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"ab31a69538694428adc66319ac89bef2","owner":"NJOGIS","created":1704828018000,"modified":1745417858000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities_in_NJ_3424","title":"MATURE SUPPORT - Colleges and Universities in NJ, 3424","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p><span>This item is in mature support and is no longer updated. Available for historical reference only.<\/span><\/p><p><span>This dataset contains the campus boundaries of Colleges and Universities of New Jersey mapped by parcel boundaries.<\/span><\/p><p><span>The Colleges and Universities dataset is composed of any type of Post Secondary Education such as: colleges, universities, technical schools, trade schools, business schools, satellite (branch) campuses, etc. that grant First Professional, Associate, Bachelors, Masters, or Doctoral degrees. Secondary education facilities, Administrative offices, or Post Secondary Education facilities that are non degree granting schools are intended to be excluded from this dataset, but a few may be included. All data is non license restricted data that has been added from TGS research.<\/span><\/p><p><\/p><p><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["Colleges and Universities","College","University"],"snippet":"This item is in mature support and is no longer updated. Available for historical reference only. The College and University file was created to help implement the NJ State Development and Redevelopment Plan by helping to identify areas where technology/health related activities and businesses could locate.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-75.4925335784916,39.097647545543985],[-73.99474130598139,41.09130108534707]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102711","accessInformation":"New Jersey Office for Planning Advocacy, NJ Office of GIS, TGS Research","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style=\"text-align:Left;\"><div><div><p><span>NEW JERSEY DEPARTMENT OF STATE, OFFICE FOR PLANNING ADVOCACY END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT.NOTICE TO USER: THIS IS A CONTRACT. USE OF THE ACCOMPANYING DATA AND/OR SOFTWARE MEANS THAT YOU ACCEPT ALL THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF THIS AGREEMENT. If you do not agree with the terms and conditions of this Agreement, erase your copy or return the software and/or data to The New Jersey Office for Planning Advocacy(OPA) without using or copying it in any way. The End User is defined as any person or organization receiving these files directly from OPA. OPA grants to the End User a license to use the software, data and documentation provided the End User agrees to the following: I. LIMITED WARRANTY: Notwithstanding the special conditions regarding the subject data specified in part III of this licensing agreement, the Office for Planning Advocacy makes no representations of any kind, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability of fitness for a particular use, nor are any such warranties to be implied, with respect to the digital software and data furnished. The Office for Planning Advocacy assumes no responsibility to maintain them in any manner or form. II. TERMS OF AGREEMENT: The data received from OPA is to be used solely by the End User and will not be reproduced or redistributed for use by anyone else, without first obtaining permission from OPA. III. SPECIAL CONDITIONS: The delineations been produced and released by the New Jersey Office for Planning Advocacy. The boundaries reflect delineations as of the date the files are posted on our website: www.nj.gov/state/planning. Any map changes accepted in the interim are not reflected in these delineations. Due to the complex nature of this mapping and the relationship of all of the individual parts of the mapping, questions regarding the the file should not be resolved by or even considered using mapping alone. For this reason, any questions relating to the mapping for the State should be directed to OPA. The information has been delivered in a standard format. OPA assumes no liability for inability of the End User to use the data/software for any financial damages caused by such an inability. OPA agrees, however, to assist in resolving any problems in using the software or data and to reproduce the data if necessary.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/XVOqAjTOJ5P6ngMu/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_in_NJ_3424/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2427,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792389600000,"source":"New Jersey Department of State, Office for Planning Advocacy","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"499c077e1b7d4c4c97269a2e6b783459","owner":"FEMA_Region9_GIS","created":1682717340000,"modified":1712883879000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Lifeline - Safety & Security - Live - Point - Colleges and Universities (IPEDS/HIFLD)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><b>Source Item:<\/b> <\/span><a href='https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=0d7bedf9d582472e9ff7a6874589b545' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=0d7bedf9d582472e9ff7a6874589b545<\/a><\/div><div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><br /><\/span><\/div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the &quot;Place Keyword&quot; section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. This release includes the addition of 130 new records, the removal of 428 no longer reported by NCES, and modifications to the spatial location and/or attribution of 6429 records.<\/span>","tags":["Education","HIFLD Open"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures Colleges and Universities defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. https://gii.dhs.gov/HIFLD","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1707852579485.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-134.97169021000653,25.428174323607433],[-99.58835487493162,46.06402496950134]],"categories":["/Categories/GeoPlatform.gov/HIFLD"],"spatialReference":"","accessInformation":"IPEDS, NCES, HIFLD, ORNL, NGA","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='margin-bottom:3rem;'><div><div style='padding-bottom:0.375rem; max-width:100%; display:inherit;'><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem;'>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/Hp6G80Pky0om7QvQ/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":15130,"scoreCompleteness":91,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792371600000,"source":"FEMA AGOL","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"0ebec9b5c8d14295ba071a66f409dc5d","owner":"ggnanaku_GIS","created":1597354448000,"modified":1597354454000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"College and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN>While each source agency classifies its facilities according to their own naming systems, we have grouped all facilities and program sites into the following seven categories to help planners navigate the data more easily:<\/SPAN><\/P><UL><LI><P><SPAN>Health and Human Services<\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN>Education, Child Welfare, and Youth<\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN>Parks, Gardens, and Historical Sites<\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN><SPAN>Libraries and Cultural Programs<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN><SPAN>Public Safety, Emergency Services, and Administration of Justice<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN><SPAN>Core Infrastructure and Transportation<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN>Administration of Government<\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><\/UL><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN>Within each of these domains, each record is further categorized into a set of facility groups, subgroups, and types that are intended to make the data easy to navigate and more useful for specific planning purposes. Facility types and names appear as they do in source datasets, wherever possible. <\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN STYLE=\"font-weight:bold;\">Notes on version 19v1:<\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN><SPAN>The code used to create the City Planning Facilities Database (FacDB) has been completely rewritten to make it more user-friendly and more maintainable. The schema has changed, as have some of the data sources. These changes are summarized below.<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN>FacDB is compiled from approximately 50 source files. Many facilities are available in more than one source file, sometimes with conflicting information. The previous version of FacDB had several fields, including CAPACITY that were formatted as strings, showing each source file that included that facility and the value contained in the source file. <\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN>In version 19v1, one source is designated as the primary source for each facility type. All values in the record come from that single source. For some facility types, like public schools or fire stations, there is an authoritative source and no secondary sources are used. For example, the Department of Education is the only source used for public schools. While other source files, such as City Owned and Leased Properties (COLP), contain records for public schools, these are not used for FacDB.<\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN>For other facility types, like day care centers, there is not a single authoritative source. One source is designated primary. All the facilities from that source are included in FacDB. If other sources include facilities at locations not in the primary source file, additional records are added to FacDB with data from the secondary source(s).<\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN STYLE=\"font-weight:bold;\">Schema changes:<\/SPAN><SPAN><SPAN>The schema has been significantly changed for version 19v1. While field names remain the same, some fields have been removed. Some fields, like CAPACITY, which were previously text fields, have been changed to numeric fields. Please review the data dictionary for the new schema.<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN STYLE=\"font-weight:bold;\">Data source changes:<\/SPAN><SPAN><SPAN>Some city agency facilities, previously sourced from COLP, have been changed to use a source file from the agency. These agency specific files are updated more frequently than COLP and provide more accurate information. Please review the data sources file for a full list of these sources and the date each was updated.<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN>Health and human services facilities formerly taken from HHS Connect are now coming from the Mayor<\/SPAN><SPAN><SPAN>\u2019<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><SPAN><SPAN>s Office of Economic Opportunity. This has resulted in a number of changes to facility categorization.<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN /><\/P><P STYLE=\"margin:0 0 0 0;\"><SPAN STYLE=\"font-weight:bold;\">Data quality improvements:<\/SPAN><SPAN><SPAN>The geocoding of facilities has been improved and there are fewer duplicate facilities.<\/SPAN><\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["Education","Facilities","2020"],"snippet":"The City Planning Facilities Database (FacDB) aggregates information about 33,000+ public and private facilities and program sites that are owned, operated, funded, licensed or certified by a City, State, or Federal agency in the City of New York. It captures facilities that generally help to shape quality of life in the city\u2019s neighborhoods and are used for planning analyses related to siting new facilities and understanding the distribution of programs and services.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-74.18075054186244,40.577862514080664],[-73.73263898291823,40.913724219204624]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"New York City Department of City Planning. Please direct feedback to DCPOpenDatal@planning.nyc.gov.","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>FacDB is only as good as the source data it aggregates, and the Department of City Planning cannot verify the accuracy of all records. Please read more about specific data and analysis limitations before using this data. Limitations include missing records, duplicate records, and the inclusion of administrative sites instead of service locations.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/ximI3fAlai1oq9BZ/arcgis/rest/services/College_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1816,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"New York City Department of City Planning","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"e0dde01f7a0e4c3db6ab92dd705af791","owner":"olivam@lattc.edu","created":1792218754000,"modified":1792377823000,"guid":null,"name":"LATTC_B01_Schools_Colleges_and_Uni","title":"Schools, Colleges and Universities - Los Angeles County (Feature Layer)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p>Public, charter and private schools, colleges and universities in Los Angeles County, with enrollment.<\/p><p><b>Why it matters:<\/b> Schools are prime sites for green schoolyards and stormwater capture, and they show where children are exposed to heat and flooding.<\/p><p>This is the <b>feature layer<\/b>: query it, filter it and read its attribute table. Its map display is the paired <a href='https://lattcarch.maps.arcgis.com//home/item.html?id=19c6c7ace8d54767beb361bf9d13606e' rel='nofollow ugc'>tile layer<\/a>.<\/p><p><b>Key fields:<\/b> Category1, Category2, Category3, Name, Label, Address Line 1, City, State, ZIP Code, Organization, Source, Source Date.<\/p><p><b>Part of:<\/b> LATTC Watershed Demo Study - Community and Environmental Justice (code B01).<\/p><p><b>Processing:<\/b> copied from the source on October 18, 2026, kept to Los Angeles County (layers over 2000 features clipped to the county land boundary), Web Mercator. <\/p><p><b>Source:<\/b> Los Angeles County Enterprise GIS / California Department of Education<\/p><ul><li><a href='https://services.arcgis.com/RmCCgQtiZLDCtblq/arcgis/rest/services/Schools_Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer/0' rel='nofollow ugc'>https://services.arcgis.com/RmCCgQtiZLDCtblq/arcgis/rest/services/Schools_Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer/0<\/a><\/li><\/ul>","tags":["LATTC Watershed Demo Study","Community and Environmental Justice","Schools","Colleges and Universities - Los Angeles County","B01","feature layer","watershed","Los Angeles"],"snippet":"Public, charter and private schools, colleges and universities in Los Angeles County, with enrollment. Schools are prime sites for green schoolyards and stormwater capture, and they show where children are exposed to heat and flooding.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-118.85415399869457,33.71348499424721],[-117.69956989860484,34.79273199940601]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Los Angeles County Enterprise GIS / California Department of Education","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"Public data from Los Angeles County Enterprise GIS / California Department of Education, republished for the LATTC Watershed Demo Study. Check the source for its terms of use and the most current version.","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services3.arcgis.com/VL3y0UFwNNVn5BNL/arcgis/rest/services/LATTC_B01_Schools_Colleges_and_Uni/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":299,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"1ebffb5cde82453488be924bf9034782","owner":"MassEOEEA","created":1650476275000,"modified":1670612411000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities   Source: MassGIS","type":"Map Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Dynamic","Map Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>Please see the <\/span><a href='https://www.mass.gov/info-details/massgis-data-colleges-and-universities' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>MassGIS metadata page<\/a><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'> for more information about this datalayer.<\/span>","tags":["higher education","college","university","RMA"],"snippet":"Higher Education Institutions in Massachusetts. Sites appearing in this layer are those normally attended by students after completion of high school. Types are public and private, and categories include co-ed, vocational, technical, religious, medical, and traditional 2- and 4-year colleges and universities.   \nSource: MassGIS ArcServer","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-73.3974,41.2903],[-70.0058,42.7974]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"26986","accessInformation":"MassGIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"None","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://arcgisserver.digital.mass.gov/arcgisserver/rest/services/AGOL/HigherEd/MapServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1578,"scoreCompleteness":96,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"source":"MA Executive Office of Energy and Environmental Affairs","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"e5d33c82ac1b43eb8c01e7d2ada61b64","owner":"WorcesterGIS","created":1742240100000,"modified":1786979492000,"guid":null,"name":"","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS","Map Service","providerSDS","Feature Access","Feature Service","ArcGIS Server","Metadata","Service","Hosted Service","Data"],"description":"<div>This dataset is a subset of the MassGIS Colleges and Universities layer. It has been projected into the <i>NAD 1983 StatePlane MA FIPS 2001 (US Feet)<\/i> coordinate system. The dataset shows the locations of institutions of higher education in Massachusetts.<\/div><div><br /><\/div><div><div><div><b>More information:<\/b> <\/div><div>Visit the <a href='https://www.mass.gov/info-details/massgis-data-colleges-and-universities' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>MassGIS Data: Colleges and Universities<\/a> webpage to learn more.<\/div><\/div><div><b><i><br /><\/i><\/b><\/div><div><span style='box-sizing:border-box; max-width:100%;'><b><i><a href='https://opendata.worcesterma.gov/' style='box-sizing:border-box; max-width:100%;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Informing Worcester<\/a><span style='box-sizing:border-box; max-width:100%;'> is the City of Worcester's open data portal where interested parties can obtain public information at no cost.<\/span><\/i><\/b><\/span><\/div><\/div>","tags":["College","University","Open Data","Geographic Data","MassGIS","Worcester","Massachusetts","United States","Infrastructure"],"snippet":"Colleges and Universities in Worcester, MA.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1742240059617.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-71.84245568424366,42.23745482149001],[-71.76159736698054,42.313854982510264]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102686","accessInformation":"MassGIS - Bureau of Geographic Information","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"Considerable effort has been made to ensure the accuracy, correctness and timeliness of data presented; however, this information is only as accurate as its sources and may not reflect the most current information. The City of Worcester, MA, assumes no liability for any errors, omissions or inaccuracies and makes no warranty, representation or guaranty of any kind, express or implied, as to the content or for any decisions made or actions taken or not taken by the user based upon any information provided with the data. The data can be freely distributed as long as the metadata entry is not modified or deleted. Any data derived from the data must acknowledge the City of Worcester, MA, in its metadata.","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/j8dqo2DJE7mVUBU1/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":"","banner":"","screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1603,"scoreCompleteness":91,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"MassGIS - Bureau of Geographic Information","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"cfabd5fb515b4b45a2714d48fbcd2dd5","owner":"WakeCountyGovernment","created":1466516599000,"modified":1771442410000,"guid":null,"name":"WakeCountyColleges","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"Wake County college and university locations","tags":["Wake County","North Carolina","schools","education","college","university","Schools","schools","Wake","NC"],"snippet":"Wake County Colleges and Universities","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-78.83499630452985,35.651572307918585],[-78.30583892788704,35.97954998528945]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"NAD_1983_StatePlane_North_Carolina_FIPS_3200_Feet","accessInformation":"Wake County GIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p>Wake County Geographic Information Services shall not be held liable for any errors in these data. This includes errors of omission, commission, errors concerning the content of the data, and relative and positional accuracy of the data. These data cannot be construed to be a legal document. Primary sources from which these data were compiled must be consulted for verification of information contained in these data.<\/p><p>License:&nbsp;<a target='_blank' href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/<\/a>&nbsp;<\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/a7CWfuGP5ZnLYE7I/arcgis/rest/services/WakeCountyColleges/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":63686,"scoreCompleteness":80,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"Wake County","licenseConstraintId":"CC-BY-4.0"},{"id":"34960d60e2eb4477a880c4b6835acee8","owner":"CommGeog","created":1391021619000,"modified":1556903189000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities in Onondaga County","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>This shapefile contains the locations of eleven 2- and 4-year, public and private colleges and universities in Onondaga County, NY. The shapefile was created in July 2012. It is projected in UTM NAD83, Zone 18 and was updated in April 2019. <\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN /><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["colleges","universities","education","higher education"],"snippet":"The Colleges and Universities shapefile was created by the Syracuse Community Geography Program. Its inteded use is for educational, research and planning using GIS.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-76.23897888849949,43.001182019816376],[-76.08764181257186,43.19063290602414]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Jonnell Robinson\nSyracuse Community Geography\n144 Eggers Hall\nSyracuse, NY 13244\nEmail: syracusecommunitygeography@gmail.com\nwww.communitygeography.org\n","classification":null,"licenseInfo":" <span>There are no access and use limitations for this \r\nitem.<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/uDTUpUPbk8X8mXwl/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_in_Onondaga_County/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":7745,"scoreCompleteness":96,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792353600000,"source":"Syracuse University","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"af292fa58e7d48b5b12aa3c8d3f6ca44","owner":"cdickes_slrusa","created":1619562979000,"modified":1782231483000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities_2017","title":"Colleges_and_Universities_2017","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com<\/span><\/a><\/p><p><span>The Colleges and Universities feature class is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, http://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2014-2015 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["facility characteristics","homeland defense","status","facility characteristics","university","enrollment","cosmetology","trade","technical","professional","trade","fine arts","secretarial","shelters","training","address","barber","barber","emergency response","Continental United States","colleges","resilience_SLR"],"snippet":"MMI Download 4/30/2018\nData Updated 1/18/2017\nSubset of National Data layer\nData Source: https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com\nClipped to City of Groton 4/27/2021 by NBS.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-72.06393526938483,41.31723109498306],[-72.06393526938483,41.31723109498306]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL) Geographic Information Science and Technology (GIST) Group, National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the datasets metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services3.arcgis.com/ZvcJEU5PM6qt0B8f/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_2017/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":158,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792393200000,"source":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"e2ad208e5a8646358a7e2933fbb01e61","owner":"ldslattery_OEMA","created":1759761279000,"modified":1761852054000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>This feature layer, utilizing data from the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories. NCES uses the&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><a style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5; text-decoration:none;' target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System&nbsp;(IPEDS)<\/span><\/span><\/a><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>&nbsp;as the \"primary source&nbsp;for information on U.S. colleges, universities, and technical and vocational institutions.\" According to&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><a style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5; text-decoration:none;' target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/datacenter/data/HD2023_Dict.zip' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>NCES<\/span><\/span><\/a><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>, this layer \"contains directory information for every institution in the 2023-24 IPEDS universe. &nbsp;Includes name, address, city, state, zip code and various URL links to the institution\"s home page, admissions, financial aid offices and &nbsp;the net price calculator. &nbsp;Identifies institutions as currently active, and institutions that participate in Title IV federal financial aid programs for which IPEDS is mandatory.\"<\/span><\/span><\/div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>&nbsp;<\/div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:center; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><img style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; display:inline; height:auto; max-width:100%;' src='https://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/ba651221e71142d8a55a09bdbb8ae13f/data' width='800' height='400' /><br /><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><i><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>University of the District of Columbia<\/span><\/i><\/span><\/div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:left; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'><strong>Data currency:<\/strong>&nbsp;2023<\/span><\/span><\/div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:left; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'><strong>Data source:&nbsp;<\/strong><\/span><\/span><a style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5; text-decoration:none;' target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/datacenter/DataFiles.aspx?year=2021&amp;sid=18837fb2-a1a9-4ce0-bb20-e8f909f3a963&amp;rtid=7' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>IPEDS Complete Data Files<\/span><\/span><\/a><\/div><div style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><div style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height:1.5;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'><strong>Data modification:<\/strong>&nbsp;Removed fields with coded values and replaced with descriptions<\/span><\/span><\/div><div style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><div style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'><strong>For more information:<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><a style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5; text-decoration:none;' target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System<\/span><\/span><\/a><\/div><div style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='color:rgb(47,79,79); font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><font style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'><strong>Support documentation: <\/strong><\/span><\/font><\/span><a style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(0, 97, 155); font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5; text-decoration:none;' target='_blank' href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/datacenter/data/HD2023_Dict.zip' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='color:rgb(52,137,197); font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><font style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>Data Dictionary<\/span><\/font><\/span><\/a><\/div><div style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='color:rgb(47,79,79); font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><font style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'><strong>For feedback, please contact:<\/strong><\/span><\/font><\/span><span style='color:rgb(77,77,77); font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><font style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/font><\/span><a style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(33, 117, 155); font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5; text-decoration:none;' href='mailto:ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com' rel='nofollow ugc'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'><font style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:inherit; line-height:1.5;'><span style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.5;'>ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com<\/span><\/font><\/span><\/a><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["university","school","college"],"snippet":"This feature layer, utilizing data from the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), displays colleges and universities in the United States and its territories. This layer is checked annually for updates.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7428,-14.3226],[171.3781,71.3247]],"categories":["/Categories/Infrastructure/Schools","/Categories/Infrastructure/Buildings"],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"U.S. Department of Education (ED)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p><span style='font-size:large;'><font style='background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; color:rgb(74, 74, 74); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.5; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><img style='border:0px solid currentcolor; box-sizing:border-box; display:inline; height:auto; max-width:100%;' src='https://downloads.esri.com/blogs/arcgisonline/esrilogo_new.png' alt='Esri logo' width='113' height