nderline;\"><SPAN>https://www.cde.ca.gov/schooldirectory/report?rid=dl1&amp;tp=txt<\/SPAN><\/A><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN>Public Schools enrollment and enhanced location:  CDE - <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com:443/home/item.html?id=98bed7e2261f47b681e9357101d7d7f7\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=98bed7e2261f47b681e9357101d7d7f7<\/SPAN><\/A><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN>Private Schools type and location:  CDE - <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://www.cde.ca.gov:443/schooldirectory/\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>https://www.cde.ca.gov/schooldirectory/<\/SPAN><\/A><SPAN>, query for <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://www.cde.ca.gov:443/SchoolDirectory/Export?exportType=ADVS&amp;format=E&amp;tab=0&amp;reqURL=%2FSchoolDirectory%2FExportSelect%3FsimpleSearch%3DN%26address%3D%26city%3D%26counties%3D%26districts%3D%26cdscode%3D%26charter%3D%26magnet%3D%26name%3D%26nps%3D%26search%3D2%26zip%3D%26yearround%3D%26status%3D1%252C2%26types%3D%26order%3D1%26multilingual%3D%26qsc%3D3466%26qdc%3D3466&amp;sd1=on&amp;sd4=on&amp;sd15=on&amp;sd51=on&amp;sd52=on\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>private schools<\/SPAN><\/A><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN>Private Schools enrollment and contact:  CDE - <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://www.cde.ca.gov:443/ds/si/ps/documents/privateschools2223.xlsx\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>https://www.cde.ca.gov/ds/si/ps/documents/privateschools2223.xlsx<\/SPAN><\/A><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN>Colleges and Universities:  HIFLD - <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com:443/datasets/geoplatform::colleges-and-universities/about\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/geoplatform::colleges-and-universities/about<\/SPAN><\/A><\/P><\/LI><\/UL><P><SPAN>Public schools use location from the <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com:443/home/item.html?id=98bed7e2261f47b681e9357101d7d7f7\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>CDE AGOL Layer<\/SPAN><\/A><SPAN> where available.  This source assigns X, Y coordinates using a quality controlled geocoding and validation process to optimize positional accuracy, often geocoding to parcel.<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-weight:bold;\">Field Descriptions:<\/SPAN><SPAN /><\/P><UL><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Category1<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  Always \"Education\"<\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN /><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Category2<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  School Level <\/SPAN><SPAN /><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Category3<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  School Type <\/SPAN><SPAN /><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Organization<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  School District for primary and secondary schools; data maintainer otherwise <\/SPAN><SPAN /><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Source<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  Source of data (see source links above) <\/SPAN><SPAN /><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Source ID<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  CDS Code for primary and secondary schools; IPEDS ID for colleges and universities <\/SPAN><SPAN /><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Source Date<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  Date listed in source <\/SPAN><SPAN /><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Enrollment<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  School Enrollment<\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><LI><P><SPAN STYLE=\"font-style:italic;\">Label Class<\/SPAN><SPAN>:  School classification for symbology (matches either Category2 or Category3)<\/SPAN><\/P><\/LI><\/UL><P><SPAN /><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["CDE","Education","Schools","Universities"],"snippet":"Primary and secondary schools, adult education, and colleges and universities. Includes public, charter, and private schools with enrollment where available.  2022-23 school year.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-118.85414000038863,33.33606887683498],[-117.69715738083644,34.795723721418845]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"California Department of Education (CDE), Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD), Los Angeles County ISD-Enterprise GIS (eGIS)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>The data herein is for informational purposes, and may not have been prepared for or be suitable for legal, engineering, or surveying intents. The County of Los Angeles reserves the right to change, restrict, or discontinue access at any time.  All users of the maps and data presented on <\/SPAN><A href=\"https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com:443/\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>https://lacounty.maps.arcgis.com<\/SPAN><\/A><SPAN> or deriving from any LA County REST URLs agree to the \"Terms of Use\" outlined on the County of LA Enterprise GIS (eGIS) Hub (<\/SPAN><A href=\"https://egis-lacounty.hub.arcgis.com:443/pages/terms-of-use\" STYLE=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><SPAN>https://egis-lacounty.hub.arcgis.com/pages/terms-of-use<\/SPAN><\/A><SPAN>).<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/2hYXmwteFLemN5bW/arcgis/rest/services/Schools_Colleges_and_Universities__1425400600956041891/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":145,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792206000000,"source":"GIS Online at UCLA","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"b6a3805a9ddb4c5bb25817740e55e308","owner":"BRADD_Admin","created":1650388403000,"modified":1753801411000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='font-size:large;'>This feature layer, utilizing data from the U.S. Department of Education (USDED), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories. The feature layer is composed of all post secondary education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) and the USDED. Included are doctoral/research universities, masters colleges and universities, baccalaureate colleges, associates colleges, theological seminaries, medical schools and other health care professions. Also included in the data are schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, law schools, teachers colleges, tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions.<\/span><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:center;'><img alt='USDED Colleges and Universities - screen capture and popup - 800x400' src='https://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/6fe8e47884df42d3919c4aabd9a9f3f6/data' style='max-width:100%; height:auto;' /><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px; text-align:center;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><i>Gallaudet University<\/i><\/font><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Data currency: see <\/font><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Colleges and Universities<\/font><\/a><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Data downloaded from: <\/font><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) &gt; <\/font><a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'>Colleges and Universities<\/font><\/a><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><div style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'>Data modification(s): none<\/span><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'>For more information: <\/span><a href='https://www.ed.gov/' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit; font-size:large;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>USDED<\/a><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'>; <\/span><a href='https://nces.ed.gov/' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit; font-size:large;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>NCES<\/a><span style='font-family:inherit; font-size:large;'>; <\/span><a href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit; font-size:large;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>IPEDS<\/a><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><font color='#000000' style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/font><\/font><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><font color='#000000' style='font-family:inherit;'>For feedback please contact:<\/font><span style='font-family:inherit; color:rgb(77, 77, 77);'> <\/span><a href='mailto:ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com' style='color:rgb(33, 117, 155); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' rel='nofollow ugc'>ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com<\/a><br /><\/font><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/font><\/div><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4' style='font-family:inherit;'><i>Thumbnail image courtesy of: <\/i><i><a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Antonio Barrera<\/a><\/i><\/font><\/div><\/div><div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><\/div><\/div>","tags":["opendata-facilities","odp-hm-facility","bradd"],"snippet":"This feature layer, utilizing data from the U.S. Department of Education, displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1650388600273.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-87.2829999999897,36.339294621976265],[-85.22899999998992,37.42899999999556]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"U.S. Department of Education (USDED); Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<font size='2'>This general-purpose content was derived from digital databases maintained by the Barren River Area Development District (BRADD) GIS Department or an external source. Care was taken in the creation and/or use of this content; however, BRADD cannot accept any responsibility for errors, omissions, or positional accuracy. There are no warranties, expressed or implied, including the warranty of merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose, accompanying this product. If errors are found in the database, please notify the BRADD GIS Department at <a href='mailto:gis@bradd.org' style='color:rgb(17, 85, 204); font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; color:rgb(0, 134, 240);'>gis@bradd.org<\/span><\/a><span style='font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; color:black;'>.<\/span><\/font>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_View/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":3892,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792368000000,"source":"Barren River Area Development District","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"cbf67cb0afff425eab4d804c62845861","owner":"bcgisdata_BCGIS","created":1746624352000,"modified":1785848733000,"guid":null,"name":"Broward_County_Colleges_And_Universities","title":"Broward County Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<b>Overview<\/b>\n<p>This feature service contains point locations for colleges and universities in Broward County, Florida, compiled from the FPL infrastructure list for 2018 and extracted from the Broward Infrastructure feature class.<\/p>\n\n<b>Content<\/b>\n<p>The layer represents higher education facilities and includes supporting attribute information such as facility name, street address, city, status, match type, premise identifier, and category details. It also includes standard record management fields for created and edited metadata.<\/p>\n\n<b>Geographic Coverage<\/b>\n<p>The data covers Broward County and supports local-scale planning, reference, and infrastructure-related GIS workflows.<\/p>\n\n<b>Use Cases<\/b>\n<ul>\n  <li>Locating colleges and universities within Broward County<\/li>\n  <li>Supporting infrastructure and service-area reference layers<\/li>\n  <li>Helping with education facility inventory and address validation<\/li>\n  <li>Providing a geographic index of higher education sites for regional analysis<\/li>\n<\/ul>","tags":["Broward County","Florida","Colleges","Universities","Higher Education","Education Facilities","School Locations","Broward","Broward County Florida","Broward County GIS","Broward Sites","Local Database Broward County","GIS","BCGIS","BC GIS","geographic","geographical","geographic analysis","geographies","local geography","county-level geography","Board of County Commissioners"],"snippet":"Point locations for colleges and universities in Broward County, Florida, compiled from the FPL infrastructure list for 2018.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-80.40418621093698,25.980301000293917],[-80.09663523515684,26.323089411777946]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"4269","accessInformation":"FPL, BCGIS, BCEMD","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/JMAJrTsHNLrSsWf5/arcgis/rest/services/Broward_County_Colleges_And_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":892,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792389600000,"source":"             Broward County GIS"},{"id":"bc5df419b76941428195b4c34180552b","owner":"tqd32886_USG","created":1787628521000,"modified":1787628550000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"HIFLD Colleges and Universities Campuses","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges point feature classes/shapefiles with a POPULATION value greater than or equal to 500. Also included is a subset of campuses with a POPULATION value under 500 or equal to -999. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Excluded are online institutions and administrative records as well as colleges and universities that do not have a verifiable campus map. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class/shapefile contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges and Colleges and Universities. Note that attribution is derived from the Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges feature classes/shapefiles. Refer to the metadata of those feature classes/shapefiles for further information regarding attribution. This release includes 21 new records and the removal of 88 records that are no longer applicable based on the sourced datasets.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","boundary","campus","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures College and University Campuses defined by the Colleges and Universities point feature class/shapefile and Supplemental Colleges point feature class/shapefile for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.744378,-14.323952],[171.378808,66.901027]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/PYn6bWCjT6bhw1z3/arcgis/rest/services/HIFLD_Colleges_and_Universities_Campuses/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":101,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"The University of Georgia ","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"892ef6fae4aa468c816cf3568be7b14a","owner":"Boston_Region_MPO","created":1628706161000,"modified":1736282723000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges_and_Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span>MassGIS COLLEGES_PT layer as a hosted feature service.<\/span><\/p><p><span>This point datalayer shows the locations of institutions of higher education in Massachusetts. Sites appearing in this layer are those normally attended by students after completion of high school. Types are public and private, and categories include co-ed, vocational, technical, religious, medical, and traditional 2- and 4-year colleges and universities. This layer was developed by MassGIS and is primarily based on all Massachusetts colleges listed in the National Center for Education Statistics website as of March 12, 2018. Additional schools were added from lists of professional occupational/vocational institutions compiled by the Massachusetts Office of Consumer Affairs and Business Regulation Division of Professional Licensure.<\/span><\/p><p><span>Data sources:<\/span><\/p><p><a href='https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/<\/span><\/a><\/p><p><a href='https://www.mass.gov/files/documents/2017/09/27/schools.pdf' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>https://www.mass.gov/files/documents/2017/09/27/schools.pdf<\/span><\/a><\/p><p><a href='https://www.mass.gov/files/documents/2018/02/15/electricians%20150-600-hrs-course-approved-schools.pdf' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>https://www.mass.gov/files/documents/2018/02/15/electricians%20150-600-hrs-course-approved-schools.pdf<\/span><\/a><\/p><p><span>Individual college websites were also consulted to verify locations and other material. MassGIS geocoded site addresses and verfied them using current ortho imagery.<\/span><\/p><p><span>A few institutions have multiple campuses, as distinct from satellite locations. For example, Harvard School of Business and Harvard Medical School are campuses within Harvard University, and a point is included in this dataset for each. Some satellite campuses may not be included. For example, Northeastern University conducts classes in satellite locations such as Milford High School. Since Milford High School is a separate educational facility, it is not considered to be a Northeastern University campus, and a point is not included in this layer.<\/span><\/p><p><span>The layer is stored in ArcSDE and distributed as COLLEGES_PT.<\/span><\/p><p><span>For pre-kindergarten through high school educational facilities, see the SCHOOL_PT layer.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["Colleges","Universities","Higher Education","Technical","Vocational","Professional","Certificate","Schools"],"snippet":"Planning, analysis, and cartographic display.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-73.39740400863444,41.290260035264424],[-70.00583276795719,42.79736262276856]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"MassGIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":{"indexJobId":""},"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/jIRgb54Jq9V3BUeD/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2469,"scoreCompleteness":75,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792303200000,"source":"MassGIS"},{"id":"071d22d61ece45eab4b6d7261917ce84","owner":"IndianaMap","created":1780335698000,"modified":1780335699000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities_2007","title":"Colleges and Universities 2007","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS","providerSDS","Feature Access","Feature Service","ArcGIS Server","Metadata","Service","Data"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>SCHOOLS_HIGHER_EDUCATION_ICHE_IN is a point shapefile showing the locations of 76 colleges and universities (including 2- and 4-year public institutions and independent institutions) listed on a directory obtained from the Indiana Commission for Higher Education (&lt;http://www.che.state.in.us/schools/interactivelist.shtml&gt;). <\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["college","colleges","university","universities","education","higher education","schools"],"snippet":"Schools - Higher Education (ICHE), 2007 - Shows the locations of 76 colleges and universities (including 2- and 4-year public institutions and independent institutions) listed on a directory obtained from the Indiana Commission for Higher Education (ICHE). Street addresses were obtained from a Web site of the ICHE (https://www.che.state.in.us/schools/interactivelist.shtml). Personnel of the Indiana University Architect's Office used geocoding to create a point shapefile. Personnel of the Indiana Geological Survey used ESRI ArcMap 9.2 to edit the locations of thirteen (13) records.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-87.71350012346892,37.944635873671075],[-84.78402419192761,41.709637190657155]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"26916","accessInformation":"It is requested that the Indiana Geological Survey be cited in any products generated from this data. The following source citation should be included: SCHOOLS_HIGHER_EDUCATION_ICHE_IN: Colleges and Universities in Indiana (Indiana Commission for Higher Education, Point Shapefile), digital representation by Theresa Thompson and Denver Harper, 2007.","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"LIMITATION OF WARRANTIES AND LIABILITY - This product is provided &quot;AS \nIS&quot;, without any other warranties or conditions, expressed or implied, \nincluding, but not limited to, warranties for product quality, or \nsuitability to a particular purpose or use. The risk or liability \nresulting from the use of this product is assumed by the user. The \nIndiana Geographic Information Office, Indiana University, and The Polis\n Center at IUPUI share no liability with product users indirect, \nincidental, special, or consequential damages whatsoever, including, but\n not limited to, loss of revenue or profit, lost or damaged data or \nother commercial or economic loss. The Indiana Geographic Information \nOffice, Indiana University, and The Polis Center at IUPUI are not \nresponsible for claims by a third party. The maximum aggregate liability\n to the original purchaser shall not exceed the amount paid by you for \nthe product.","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://gisdata.in.gov/server/rest/services/Hosted/Colleges_and_Universities_2007/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":"","banner":"","screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":350,"scoreCompleteness":95,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"Indiana Commission for Higher Education","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"8d9c91bedea547738c0a408a8fc14bea","owner":"FEMA_Region9_GIS","created":1664234563000,"modified":1701892059000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Lifeline - Safety & Security - Static - Point - 2019 / Colleges and Universities (IPEDS/HIFLD)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><b>Source Item:<\/b> <a href='https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=0d7bedf9d582472e9ff7a6874589b545' style='color:rgb(0, 97, 155); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:inherit;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=0d7bedf9d582472e9ff7a6874589b545<\/a><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><br /><\/div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the &quot;Place Keyword&quot; section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. This release includes the addition of 130 new records, the removal of 428 no longer reported by NCES, and modifications to the spatial location and/or attribution of 6429 records.<\/span>","tags":["Critical Infrastructure"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures Colleges and Universities defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. https://gii.dhs.gov/HIFLD. 2019 snapshot.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1701891899673.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-134.9999999999977,24.999999999999563],[-99.99999999999831,44.99999999999924]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"","accessInformation":"IPEDS, NCES, HIFLD, ORNL, NGA","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='margin-bottom:3rem;'><div><div style='padding-bottom:0.375rem; max-width:100%; display:inherit;'><div style='margin-bottom:3rem;'><div style='padding-bottom:0.375rem; max-width:100%; display:inherit;'><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem;'>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/XG15cJAlne2vxtgt/arcgis/rest/services/Critical_Infrastructure_Map_Service/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2344,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1790359200000,"source":"FEMA AGOL","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"1066e7227a9448c49274880121a7192a","owner":"cgmcgove","created":1605648202000,"modified":1767044630000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"Colleges and Universities.<div><br /><\/div><div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>For more information, contact: GIS Manager Information Technology &amp; Innovation (ITI) Montgomery County Planning Department, MNCPPC T: 301-650-5620<\/span><br /><\/div>","tags":["Education","Colleges","Universities","Montgomery County Planning Department","Montgomery County","MNCPPC","Maryland"],"snippet":"Locations of Colleges and Universities in Montgomery County, MD.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1626789848533.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-77.2468,38.9842],[-76.9656,39.1878]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Montgomery County Department of Technology & Enterprise Business Solutions","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"You can copy, modify, distribute, and perform analysis on the data, even for commercial purposes, all without asking permission, but please provide attribution to the Montgomery County Planning Department. The Planning Department makes no warranties about the data, and disclaims liability for all uses of the data, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://mcmaps.org/server11/rest/services/Overlays/MCAtlas_Educational_Facilities/MapServer/6","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1847,"scoreCompleteness":93,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"Montgomery Maps","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"eec39d4509b24514a69dbed7b1d53ad7","owner":"jia.fang@dot.state.fl.us_fdot","created":1772215331000,"modified":1788271191000,"guid":null,"name":"Florida_Colleges_and_Universities","title":"Florida Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p style=\"color:#4A4A4A; font-family:inherit; font-size:12.0pt; margin:0in;\">This layer is used in the Florida Trends and Conditions&nbsp;Dashboard which provides an outlook for the state and walks through key items affecting Florida\u2019s current and future transportation challenges. The regional stories highlight the trends, opportunities, and challenges impacting areas throughout the State of Florida.<\/p><p style=\"font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;; font-size:12.0pt; margin:0in;\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.fdot.gov/planning/ftp/default.shtm\">https://www.fdot.gov/planning/ftp/default.shtm<\/a><\/p>","tags":["FDOT","FTP"],"snippet":"This layer visualizes Florida Colleges and Universities.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-88.022461,24.327077],[-78.42041,31.16581]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"2883","accessInformation":"Florida Department of Transportation - System Forecasting & Trends Office","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p style=\"font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.0pt;margin:0in;\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana;\">NO WARRANTIES: This site and its content is made available by the Florida Department of Transportation on an \"as is\", \"as available\" basis without warranties of any kind, express or implied. DISCLAIMER OF LIABILITY: The user of this application and data assumes all responsibility and risk for the use of both. Under no circumstances, including negligence, shall the Florida Department of Transportation, or its employees be liable for any DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY or CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES, or LOST PROFITS that result from the use, misuse or inability to use the application and data. Nor shall the Florida Department of Transportation, or its employees be liable for any damages resulting from or related to reliance; mistakes, omissions, interruptions, deletion of files, computer viruses, errors, defects, or any failure of performance, communications failure, theft, destruction or unauthorized access to the application and data.<\/span><\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/O1JpcwDW8sjYuddV/arcgis/rest/services/Florida_Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1429,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"Florida Department of Transportation","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"934685751ea541db83292fabd032b9eb","owner":"JustinFrye_ColliersGIS","created":1733509020000,"modified":1733509035000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges_and_Universities_2494650739437433648","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, http://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. This release includes the addition of 130 new records, the removal of 428 no longer reported by NCES, and modifications to the spatial location and/or attribution of 6429 records.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["Colleges 2024"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures Colleges and Universities defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://gii.dhs.gov/HIFLD)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.743181,-14.323164],[171.378453,71.324727]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><P><SPAN>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services8.arcgis.com/6BLwQZQlYNgkh7e7/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_2494650739437433648/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":242,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792288800000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"2332b3be52ba4c6aad25faa415e22024","owner":"gabrielle.jones@indianaffairs.gov_BIA_Geospatial","created":1753208205000,"modified":1755629211000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCU) Web Map","type":"Web Map","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Online","Explorer Web Map","Map","Metadata","Online Map","Web Map"],"description":"<p>Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs) are chartered by their respective tribal governments, including the ten tribes within the largest reservations in the United States. The 33 accredited TCUs operate more than 90 campuses and sites in 15 states\u2014covering most of Indian Country\u2014and serve students from well more than 250 federally recognized Indian tribes. TCUs vary in enrollment (size), focus (liberal arts, sciences, workforce development/training), location (woodlands, desert, frozen tundra, rural, urban), and student population (predominantly American Indian). However, tribal identity is the core of every TCU, and they all share the mission of tribal self-determination and service to their respective communities.<\/p><p>These academically rigorous institutions engage in partnerships with organizations including U.S. Department of the Interior, U.S. Department of Agriculture, U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, the National Science Foundation, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, and universities nationwide to support research and education programs that focus on issues such as climate change, sustainable agriculture, water quality, wildlife population dynamics, and diabetes prevention. Many support distance learning involving state-of-the-art learning environments.<\/p>","tags":["BOGS","Pathways"],"snippet":"Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs) are a category of Minority Serving Institutions in the United States higher education system. They are distinguished as tribal schools because they are chartered by tribal governments and are located on or near American Indian reservations.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.934305,12.725041],[-54.074484,72.245342]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"","accessInformation":"Bureau of Indian Affairs, Branch of Geospatial Support (BOGS), BIA Pathways Program, Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database.","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div>No warranty is made by the Bureau of Indian Affairs (BIA) for the use of the data for purposes not intended by the BIA. This GIS Dataset may contain errors. There is no impact on the legal status of the land areas depicted herein and no impact on land ownership. No legal inference can or should be made from the information in this GIS Dataset. The GIS Dataset is prepared strictly for illustrative and reference purposes only and should not be used, and is not intended for legal, survey, engineering or navigation purposes. <\/div><div><br /><\/div><div>These data have been developed from the best available sources. Although efforts have been made to ensure that the data are accurate and reliable, errors and variable conditions originating from source documents and/or the translation of information from source documents to the systems of record continue to exist. Users must be aware of these conditions and bear responsibility for the appropriate use of the information with respect to possible errors, scale, resolution, rectification, positional accuracy, development methodology, time period, environmental and climatic conditions and other circumstances specific to these data. The user is responsible for understanding the accuracy limitations of the data provided herein. The burden for determining fitness for use lies entirely with the user. The user should refer to the accompanying metadata notes for a description of the data and data development procedures. <\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1087,"scoreCompleteness":91,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792360800000,"source":"Bureau of Indian Affairs","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"20f78ef8125a46e9b866b11d3213ad37","owner":"1801363_CAL","created":1786058920000,"modified":1786060271000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"colleges_and_universities_campuses_shapefile","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges point feature classes/shapefiles with a POPULATION value greater than or equal to 500. Also included is a subset of campuses with a POPULATION value under 500 or equal to -999. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Excluded are online institutions and administrative records as well as colleges and universities that do not have a verifiable campus map. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class/shapefile contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges and Colleges and Universities. Note that attribution is derived from the Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges feature classes/shapefiles. Refer to the metadata of those feature classes/shapefiles for further information regarding attribution. This release includes 21 new records and the removal of 88 records that are no longer applicable based on the sourced datasets.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","boundary","campus","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures College and University Campuses defined by the Colleges and Universities point feature class/shapefile and Supplemental Colleges point feature class/shapefile for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.744378,-14.323952],[171.378808,66.901027]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/iq8zYa0SRsvIFFKz/arcgis/rest/services/colleges_and_universities_campuses_shapefile/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":23,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"b973b8b50b234711b5fe7b759c60dbe0","owner":"FEMA_Region_6_GIS","created":1718642300000,"modified":1728483795000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Lifeline - Safety & Security - Live - Point - Colleges and Universities (HIFLD)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div>Source: <a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.hub.arcgis.com/datasets/geoplatform::colleges-and-universities/about' rel='nofollow ugc'>Colleges and Universities | HIFLD (arcgis.com)<\/a><\/div><div><br /><\/div>The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2019-2020 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions.<div><br /><\/div><div>Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class (<a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.hub.arcgis.com/datasets/geoplatform::supplemental-colleges/about' rel='nofollow ugc'>Supplemental Colleges | HIFLD (arcgis.com)<\/a>) when found. <\/div>","tags":["Education","college","university","postgraduate","lifeline","safety","security","region 6","r6"],"snippet":"Location of Colleges and Universities as provided by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. Data filtered to FEMA Region 6 states.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1728483794010.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.743174585,-14.323171423999941],[171.37844200000004,71.32470200000006]],"categories":["/Categories/Safety and Security"],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"HIFLD","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/Hp6G80Pky0om7QvQ/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":909,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792360800000,"source":"FEMA AGOL"},{"id":"76eb5474cc1548d69d2f4a0fe76d4e3e","owner":"gabrielle.jones@indianaffairs.gov_BIA_Geospatial","created":1753372734000,"modified":1755628987000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCU) Dashboard","type":"Dashboard","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Dashboards","Dashboard","Metadata","Mobile","Operations Dashboard"],"description":"<p>Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs) are higher education institutions that are operated tribally or by the Bureau of Indian Education (BIE) and primarily function to serve Native American communities. They are often located on or near reservations and play an important role in preserving Native American culture while providing academic or vocational training, typically at an affordable price.<\/p><p><br />The Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCU) Layer contains addresses, leadership information, contact details, addresses, and coordinates for each of the institutions recognized by the BIE.<\/p>","tags":["BIA","BIE","Colleges","Universities","Schools","Education","Higher Education"],"snippet":"The Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCU) Dashboard contains addresses, leadership information, contact details, addresses, and coordinates for each institution recognized by the BIE.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1755625940188.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-169.961556,21.791156],[-61.16897,71.940398]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"","accessInformation":"Bureau of Indian Affairs, Bureau of Indian Education","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p>No warranty is made by the Bureau of Indian Affairs (BIA) for the use of the data for purposes not intended by the BIA. This GIS Dataset may contain errors. There is no impact on the legal status of the land areas depicted herein and no impact on land ownership. No legal inference can or should be made from the information in this GIS Dataset. The GIS Dataset is prepared strictly for illustrative and reference purposes only and should not be used, and is not intended for legal, survey, engineering or navigation purposes. These data have been developed from the best available sources. Although efforts have been made to ensure that the data are accurate and reliable, errors and variable conditions originating from source documents and/or the translation of information from source documents to the systems of record continue to exist. Users must be aware of these conditions and bear responsibility for the appropriate use of the information with respect to possible errors, scale, resolution, rectification, positional accuracy, development methodology, time period, environmental and climatic conditions and other circumstances specific to these data. The user is responsible for understanding the accuracy limitations of the data provided herein. The burden for determining fitness for use lies entirely with the user. The user should refer to the accompanying metadata notes for a description of the data and data development procedures<\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":643,"scoreCompleteness":98,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792360800000,"source":"Bureau of Indian Education Office of Communications","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"fae2ebd572964895a0e953616d8aa911","owner":"CDPHE_user_community","created":1744915371000,"modified":1788383830000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"CDPHE Colorado College and University Immunization Data","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Table"],"description":"<p>The Colorado Department of Public Health and Environment (CDPHE) Colorado College and University Immunization Data table contains data displayed in the Colorado School and Childcare Immunization Data <a target='_blank' href='https://cdphe.colorado.gov/immunization/school-and-child-care-data' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Dashboard<\/a>, beginning with the 2010-2011 school year.<\/p><p>The CDPHE Immunization Program annually collects immunization data from Colorado universities and colleges that meet the requirement to report aggregate immunization data. &nbsp;This dataset does not include data for school years when a specific college or university did not report their data to CDPHE. The datasets are updated annually when the most recently collected school year data is ready for publication, usually in late spring.<\/p><p>Per Colorado Board of Health rule <a target='_blank' href='https://www.sos.state.co.us/CCR/DisplayRule.do?action=ruleinfo&amp;ruleId=2416&amp;deptID=16&amp;agencyID=142&amp;deptName=1000%20Public%20Health%20and%20Environment&amp;agencyName=1009%20Disease%20Control%20and%20Environmental%20Epidemiology%20Division&amp;seriesNum=6%20CCR%201009-2' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>6 CCR 1009-2<\/a>, students attending Colorado colleges or universities that have residence hall facilities within their systems have two requirements. &nbsp;The measles, mumps, and rubella vaccine (MMR) requirement applies to college or university students who are enrolled in one or more classes and will be physically present at a college or university for participation in classes, athletics, or other activities. &nbsp;This includes students who are auditing classes but does not include nontraditional adult students as defined by the governing board of the institution or persons taking classes online or by correspondence only. &nbsp;The meningococcal requirement applies to new first year college or university students who will reside in student housing. &nbsp;The <a target='_blank' href='https://cdphe.colorado.gov/immunization/resources-for-child-care-schools-colleges/guidance-resources' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>college and university school-required immunization guidance and resources<\/a> webpage has information on immunization requirements to attend school in Colorado.<\/p><p>Here is a brief description of the fields included in this dataset:<\/p><ul><li>Year: This field indicates the school year of the survey data (e.g. 2023/2024) (character).<\/li><li>Name: This field indicates the name of the college or university. For statewide values, the value is \u2018Statewide\u2019 (character).&nbsp;<\/li><li>Vaccine: This field indicates either MMR or Meningococcal (MenACWY) vaccination data. (character).&nbsp;<\/li><li>Student_Population: This field indicates the grade level. &nbsp;<ul><li>For MMR, values include All grade levels, Freshmen, Sophomore, Junior, Senior, Graduate, and Other. &nbsp;<\/li><li>For Meningococcal, the value is \u2018Total new students residing in student housing\u2019 (character).&nbsp;<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Metric: This field indicates the vaccination status category. &nbsp;<ul><li>For MMR, values include Enrollment, Fully Immunized, Medical Exemption, Nonmedical Exemption, In Process, Incomplete Record, and No Record. &nbsp;<\/li><li>For Meningococcal (MenACWY), values include Enrollment, Fully Immunized, Signed Waiver, Incomplete Record, and No Record (character). &nbsp;<\/li><li>The <a target='_blank' href='https://drive.google.com/file/d/1r6Ufc52dwy2zgq1rchsIcDCyExFllWt6/view' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>College/University reporting worksheet<\/a> has definitions of the metrics included in this dataset. &nbsp;<\/li><li>CDPHE began collecting information about college or university students with an incomplete record in the 2023/24 school year. &nbsp;<\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>Value: &nbsp;This field indicates the student enrollment or vaccination status rate.<\/li><\/ul>","tags":["Colorado","SCCIDR","School and Child Care Immunization Data Reporting","College","University","CDPHE","Immunization"],"snippet":"","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1747174155863.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-2.0E7,-2.0E7],[2.0E7,2.0E7]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Colorado Department of Public Health and Environment","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"These data are published for informational purposes and there are no restrictions for using or disseminating this data set.  Users of the data should consider factors such as the data source, time period, assignment of geography, statistical reliability, and/or calculation of rate.  The State of Colorado and the Colorado Department of Public Health and Environment assumes no liability to the completeness, correctness, or fitness for use of this data set.  Please contact the  Colorado Department of Public Health and Environment using this website if you require more information on how these data were assembled.","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://www.cohealthmaps.dphe.state.co.us/arcgis/rest/services/OPEN_DATA/cdphe_sccidr/MapServer/3","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":3468,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792386000000,"source":"Colorado Department of Public Health and Environment","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"c4838a970e4d4c8a8400f893360fd4c7","owner":"agoladmin_septa","created":1743506588000,"modified":1743696336000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":null,"tags":["Education"],"snippet":"Colleges and Universities in the SEPTA service area","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-75.96865770078601,39.74169399997312],[-74.65225399954976,40.67583499956158]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/9U43PSoL47wawX5S/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":468237,"scoreCompleteness":46,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792382400000,"source":"SEPTA Web Mapping Portal"},{"id":"2d9d3a60794f49fa987fe5c32fb7f384","owner":"tga_admin01","created":1574883696000,"modified":1574885314000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges_and_Universities_Campuses","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;; font-size:18px; background-color:rgb(248, 248, 248);'>The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges point feature classes/shapefiles with a POPULATION value above 500. Also included is a subset of campuses with a POPULATION value under 500 or equal to -999. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class/shapefile contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the &quot;Place Keyword&quot; section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges and Colleges and Universities. Note that attribution is derived from the Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges feature classes/shapefiles. Refer to the metadata of those feature classes/shapefiles for further information regarding attribution. This release includes 6005 records.<\/span>","tags":["HIFLD","infrastructure","Schools","College","University"],"snippet":"The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7444,-14.324],[171.3788,66.901]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities-campuses","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/Hp6G80Pky0om7QvQ/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_Campuses/FeatureServer/0","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":644,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1788112800000,"source":"Tennessee Geographic Alliance"},{"id":"7c4e88c2ae474b999ab2959ffff5107d","owner":"nataliekim_UMass_Amherst","created":1741644965000,"modified":1751592058000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities in Massachusetts ","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<DIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"><DIV><DIV><P><SPAN>This point datalayer shows the locations of institutions of higher education in Massachusetts. Sites appearing in this layer are those normally attended by students after completion of high school. Types are public and private, and categories include co-ed, vocational, technical, religious, medical, and traditional 2- and 4-year colleges and universities. This layer was developed by MassGIS and is primarily based on all Massachusetts colleges listed in the National Center for Education Statistics website as of November 21, 2023. Additional schools were added from lists of professional occupational/vocational institutions compiled by the Massachusetts Office of Consumer Affairs and Business Regulation Division of Professional Licensure.<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>Data sources:<\/SPAN><\/P><P><A href=\"https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/\"><SPAN>https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/<\/SPAN><\/A><\/P><P><SPAN>https://www.mass.gov/doc/approved-initial-education-providers-for-electricians<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>Individual college websites were also consulted to verify locations and other material. MassGIS geocoded site addresses and verfied them using current ortho imagery.<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>A few institutions have multiple campuses, as distinct from satellite locations. For example, Harvard School of Business and Harvard Medical School are campuses within Harvard University, and a point is included in this dataset for each. Some satellite campuses may not be included. For example, Northeastern University conducts classes in satellite locations such as Milford High School. Since Milford High School is a separate educational facility, it is not considered to be a Northeastern University campus, and a point is not included in this layer.<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>The layer is stored in ArcSDE and distributed as COLLEGES_PT.<\/SPAN><\/P><P><SPAN>For pre-kindergarten through high school educational facilities, see the SCHOOL_PT layer.<\/SPAN><\/P><\/DIV><\/DIV><\/DIV>","tags":["Colleges","Universities","Higher Education","Technical","Vocational","Professional","Certificate","Schools"],"snippet":"Planning, analysis, and cartographic display.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1751592071433.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-73.398823,41.290252],[-70.004714,42.844343]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"MassGIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/2gdL2gxYNFY2TOUb/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_in_Massachusetts_/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":449,"scoreCompleteness":75,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792375200000,"source":"MassGIS"},{"id":"51bc10d177a84d408b28438c4ef6090d","owner":"Jay.puckett_wsp5","created":1750887726000,"modified":1785965726000,"guid":null,"name":"College_University_1_1","title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p>This feature service contains a community services and facilities layer for the City of Santa Fe focused on college and university locations. It provides point features representing higher education facilities that can support city planning, public information, and location-based reference application. Identified by school name, facility type, and address.<\/p>","tags":["Santa Fe","colleges","universities","higher education","community facilities","schools","New Mexico"],"snippet":"A community services and facilities layer showing college and university locations in Santa Fe.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-106.05270832848998,35.5864280809962],[-105.91154758783807,35.66712916371159]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102713","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services7.arcgis.com/p0Gk2nDbPs7KEqSZ/arcgis/rest/services/College_University_1/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":513,"scoreCompleteness":80,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792375200000,"source":"City of Santa Fe"},{"id":"37c5b0cd29e34aeb9406d120928e89f6","owner":"ShanePavlak","created":1774978920000,"modified":1774979016000,"guid":null,"name":"","title":"Colleges and Universities Locations","type":"Map Service","typeKeywords":["Map Service","ArcGIS Server","Metadata","Service","Data"],"description":"<p><strong>Overview<\/strong><\/p><p>This feature service provides spatial data representing the locations of colleges and universities within Ottawa County. It offers detailed point location data for post-secondary educational institutions in this specific region.<\/p><p><strong>Feature Layers<\/strong><\/p><ul><li><strong>Colleges<\/strong>: This layer displays the point locations of colleges and universities throughout Ottawa County. It includes attributes such as institution names and metadata about dataset creation and editing to support data management and traceability.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Geographic Coverage<\/strong><\/p><p>The dataset is focused on Ottawa County, providing a regional view of higher education institution locations within this geographic boundary.<\/p><p><strong>Use Cases<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Supporting educational planning and analysis by local governments or educational authorities.<\/li><li>Providing location data for mapping and visualization of higher education facilities.<\/li><li>Assisting prospective students or researchers in identifying college and university locations in the area.<\/li><\/ul>","tags":["Political","Education","College","University"],"snippet":"This service features point locations of colleges and universities in Ottawa County, useful for educational planning and analysis.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-86.1072437175441,42.7791229965567],[-85.8852277500893,42.9664886474572]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"WGS_1984_Web_Mercator_Auxiliary_Sphere","accessInformation":"Ottawa County GIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://gis.miottawa.org/arcgis/rest/services/HostedServices/Colleges/MapServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":"","banner":"","screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":12,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"ixRLoNIl4gmM9jgg","scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1790992800000,"source":"Ottawa County Geospatial Insights & Solutions"},{"id":"276d5df38d3c4883bdb47e98f300e667","owner":"FairfaxCounty","created":1698851265000,"modified":1770662420000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Greater Washington - Colleges and Universities","type":"StoryMap","typeKeywords":["arcgis-storymaps","smdraftresourceid:draft_1770662419098.json","smfirstpublisheddate:1698865648595","smpublisheddate:1770662419098","smstatuspublished","smversiondraft:26.5.1183","smversionpublished:26.5.1183","StoryMap","Web Application"],"description":"<p>The Greater Washington - Colleges and Universities app is a dynamic tool designed to streamline the search for higher education options in the Washington D.C. metropolitan area. This comprehensive app caters not only to students but also serves as a valuable resource for companies scouting talent and veterans seeking to upskill.<\/p><p>Whether you're a student, a company seeking talent, or a veteran aiming to upskill, this app is your go-to resource for navigating the diverse educational landscape of Greater Washington.<\/p>","tags":["FFX","Fairfax County","Virginia","VA"],"snippet":"Fairfax County Economic Development Authority","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.jpeg","documentation":null,"extent":[],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Fairfax County, Virginia; Economic Development Authority","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='background-image:initial; background-position:initial; background-size:initial; background-repeat:initial; background-attachment:initial; background-origin:initial; background-clip:initial; color:rgb(9, 31, 47); font-size:11.5pt; font-family:Helvetica, sans-serif;'>Please review the <\/span><span style='background-image:initial; background-position:initial; background-size:initial; background-repeat:initial; background-attachment:initial; background-origin:initial; background-clip:initial; color:rgb(9, 31, 47); font-size:11.5pt; font-family:Helvetica, sans-serif;'><a href='https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/maps/disclaimer' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Fairfax County GIS Division disclaimer<\/a><\/span>","culture":"en","properties":{"thumbnail":["url","https://su.example/content/items/276d5df38d3c4883bdb47e98f300e667/resources/DDpcQMFyZhX2fhouphDoo.jpeg{{qp|[[\"wago\"],[\"ust\"]]}}"],"metaProperties":{"title":"Greater Washington - Colleges and Universities","description":"Fairfax County Economic Development Authority"},"shouldHideCover":false},"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/276d5df38d3c4883bdb47e98f300e667","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1810,"scoreCompleteness":90,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792231200000,"source":"County of Fairfax","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"865495cf9074421cb4a0578c9f7caaf2","owner":"WVatlas","created":1561747315000,"modified":1572595780000,"guid":null,"name":"WV_Colleges_and_Univ_","title":"WV Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p><span style='font-size: medium;'>The data in this layer was obtained through UCLA Geoportal <\/span><a href='https://gis.ucla.edu/geodata/'>https://gis.ucla.edu/geodata/<\/a>.<br /><\/p><p>This data layer is provided for educational purposes only.\nThese data are not to be used for navigation. These data are believed to be\naccurate, but the accuracy of these data is not guaranteed. While WVDE has\nattempted to ensure that the information in this data layer is accurate, WVDE\ndoes not assume any liability for any errors, omissions, or inaccuracies in the\ninformation provided regardless of the usage taken by the use of the data\nlater.<\/p>\n\n<p> <\/p>\n\n<p>Use of this data layer assumes that you understand and agree\nwith the information provided in this disclaimer.<\/p>\n\n<p> <\/p>\n\n<p>Any errors, omissions, or other questions regarding this\ndata layer can be reported to Erika Klose, eklose@k12.wv.us.<\/p>","tags":["WV Atlas"],"snippet":"WV Colleges","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1563818139687.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-82.44306010773772,37.26688046755958],[-77.80484384296892,40.53274875664988]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"WGS84(DD)","accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/xdbDcZrQnv51VAwh/arcgis/rest/services/WV_Colleges_and_Univ_/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1378,"scoreCompleteness":53,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792382400000,"source":"WVDE Atlas for Students and Educators"},{"id":"9ee6ca49ccce4928bcf235904689d2c0","owner":"Surenderreddy.Konatham@flhealth.gov_FDOH","created":1466108572000,"modified":1513198522000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"College and University Tobacco Policies in FL- Updated 12-13-2017","type":"Web Map","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Online","Collector","Data Editing","Explorer Web Map","Map","Offline","Online Map","Web Map"],"description":"<span style='overflow: auto;'><span>This map displays tobacco policy data and school information for colleges and universities in the state of Florida. Additionally, the user can interactively filter (a) college types, (b) policy types, and (c) counties for more in-depth examination.<\/span><\/span>","tags":["Tobacco","College","University","School","Policy"],"snippet":"Displays tobacco policy data and school information for colleges and universities in the state of Florida.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-89.7649,29.2522],[-76.5045,31.6481]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"DOH Alachua (Parker Hinson, Andrew Romero, Jessie King, John-Michael Gonzales); Bureau of Tobacco Free Florida (Erin Singerman and BTFF Grantees)","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":null,"proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1776,"scoreCompleteness":78,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791900000000,"source":"Florida Department of Health"},{"id":"7dfb704da2fd4c01955bef68b85c938a","owner":"MassGIS","created":1777349525000,"modified":1779917249000,"guid":null,"name":"Colleges_and_Universities","title":"Colleges and Universities (Hosted Feature Layer)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;font-size:12pt'><div><div><p><span>The locations of institutions of higher education in Massachusetts. Sites appearing in this layer are those normally attended by students after completion of high school. Types are public and private, and categories include co-ed, vocational, technical, religious, medical, and traditional 2- and 4-year colleges and universities.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["Colleges","Universities","Higher Education","Technical","Vocational","Professional","Certificate","Schools","MassGIS","Massachusetts"],"snippet":"Colleges and universities in Massachusetts","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1779917247565.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-73.32591840052079,41.29140408501517],[-70.0047144227565,42.844351375273234]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"26986","accessInformation":"MassGIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/hGdibHYSPO59RG1h/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1204,"scoreCompleteness":71,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"source":"MassGIS - Bureau of Geographic Information"},{"id":"d108df06eac14d3981385022ee1eedbe","owner":"layermanager","created":1711631426000,"modified":1718389119000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>This feature layer, utilizing data from the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories. This layer contains directory information for every institution in the 2021-22 IPEDS universe. Includes name, address, city, state, zip code and various URL links to the institution's home page, admissions, financial aid offices and the net price calculator. Identifies institutions as currently active, institutions that participate in Title IV federal financial aid programs for which IPEDS is mandatory. It also includes variables derived from the 2021-22 Institutional Characteristics survey, such as control and level of institution, highest level and highest degree offered and Carnegie classifications.<\/span>","tags":[""],"snippet":"","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1715715625041.png","documentation":null,"extent":[],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_View/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1193323,"scoreCompleteness":50,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"source":"GIS WebTech"},{"id":"1394411a4e0144929a8cbeb580df5906","owner":"Andy.Venuto_GOHSEP","created":1597246083000,"modified":1597246165000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"HIFLD Louisiana Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"This feature class links to the HIFLD Open Data Private Schools layer and filters by Louisiana. The source data and description can be found here: <a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities' rel='nofollow ugc'>https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/colleges-and-universities<\/a><div><br /><\/div><div>HIFLD Open Data Portal: <a href='https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/' rel='nofollow ugc'>https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/<\/a><\/div>","tags":["HIFLD","Colleges","Universities","Louisiana"],"snippet":"This feature class links to the HIFLD Colleges and Universites layer and filters on Louisiana.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7432,-14.3232],[171.3784,71.3247]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"HIFLD","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/Hp6G80Pky0om7QvQ/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer/0","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":1453,"scoreCompleteness":78,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791709200000,"source":"Louisiana Homeland Security and Emergency Preparedness"},{"id":"a84932e949ae477e9b455a784c0a9904","owner":"cai14307@esri.com_government_admin","created":1786739632000,"modified":1789590616000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<b>Overview<\/b>\n<p>This feature service contains point locations for colleges and universities, along with institutional attributes that describe each campus. The data supports search, display, and analysis of higher education facilities and their basic characteristics.<\/p>\n\n<b>Content<\/b>\n<p>The layer includes college and university point features with information about institution type, ownership or control, size, level of instruction offered, and special institutional designations. It also provides standard location and contact details such as campus name, address, city, state, ZIP code, website, and general phone number.<\/p>\n\n<b>Geographic Coverage<\/b>\n<p>The feature extent indicates coverage across a regional area in the western United States, supporting mapping and reference use for higher education institutions within that area.<\/p>\n\n<b>Use Cases<\/b>\n<ul>\n  <li>Locating colleges and universities on a map<\/li>\n  <li>Supporting higher education planning and reference applications<\/li>\n  <li>Identifying institutional characteristics such as public or private control and degree level<\/li>\n  <li>Displaying campus contact and website information in GIS applications<\/li>\n<\/ul>","tags":["colleges","universities","higher education","campus locations","education institutions","western United States"],"snippet":"Point locations for colleges and universities with institutional and contact information for higher education reference and mapping.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1787343707697.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-114.71155800033202,31.5645970002588],[-102.616143999558,44.7639259998836]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services5.arcgis.com/P4wLr24CKpw9X4c3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":41,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792321200000,"source":"Esri State & Local Government Online - SBO"},{"id":"632d8aaf141e48b3a5ebecea5417bc67","owner":"cityharveststaff","created":1437358579000,"modified":1437725285000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<table border='0' cellpadding='0' cellspacing='0' style='border-collapse:\r\n collapse;width:603pt' width='803'>\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n <tbody><tr height='21' style='height:15.75pt'>\r\n  <td height='21' style='height:15.75pt;width:91pt' width='121'>DATA<\/td>\r\n  <td style='width:13pt' width='17'>:<\/td>\r\n  <td style='width:499pt' width='665'>Colleges and Universities<\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr height='21' style='height:15.75pt'>\r\n  <td height='21' style='height:15.75pt;border-top:none'>SOURCE<\/td>\r\n  <td>:<\/td>\r\n  <td>NYC Department of Information Technology &amp;\r\n  Telecommunications (DoITT)<\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr height='21' style='height:15.75pt'>\r\n  <td height='21' style='height:15.75pt;border-top:none'>DATE UPDATED<\/td>\r\n  <td>:<\/td>\r\n  <td>11/17/2014<\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr height='21' style='height:15.75pt'>\r\n  <td height='21' style='height:15.75pt;border-top:none'>DATE ACQUIRED<\/td>\r\n  <td>:<\/td>\r\n  <td>6/23/2015<\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr height='21' style='height:15.75pt'>\r\n  <td height='21' style='height:15.75pt;border-top:none'>LINK<\/td>\r\n  <td>:<\/td>\r\n  <td><a href='https://data.cityofnewyork.us/Education/Colleges-and-Universities/4kym-4xw5'><span style='color:black;font-size:10.0pt;text-decoration:none;font-family:&quot;Calibri Light&quot;, sans-serif;\r\n  mso-font-charset:0'>https://data.cityofnewyork.us/Education/Colleges-and-Universities/4kym-4xw5<\/span><\/a><\/td>\r\n <\/tr><\/tbody><\/table>","tags":["college","university","higher education","education","new york"],"snippet":"NYC Colleges and Universities","thumbnail":"thumbnail/colleges.PNG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-74.14957647577573,40.600485043535095],[-73.75702081562804,40.91268859320588]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/84qHOn0KfgcVU3ZD/arcgis/rest/services/COLLEGE_UNIVERSITY/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":5189,"scoreCompleteness":71,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792162800000,"source":"City Harvest"},{"id":"e157eba4beff4333b7a109701a3ba919","owner":"s651545_SPPS","created":1559134875000,"modified":1559134876000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities - copy","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4'>The feature layer is composed of all post secondary education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES) and the USDED for the 2013-2014 school year. Included are doctoral/research universities, masters colleges and universities, baccalaureate colleges, associates colleges, theological seminaries, medical schools and other health care professions, schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, law schools, teachers colleges, tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions.<\/font><\/span><div style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;'><font size='4'><br /><\/font><div style='text-align: center;'><font size='4'><img alt='USDED Colleges and Universities - screen capture and popup' src='http://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/2c85e70fdd6c41c78678044e234e947b/data' /><br /><\/font><\/div><div style='text-align: center;'><i><font size='4'>Colleges and Universities<\/font><\/i><\/div><div style=''><font size='4'>Data currency: 2013-2014<\/font><\/div><div style=''><font size='4'>For more information: <a href='https://www.ed.gov/' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration: none;' target='_blank'>USDED<\/a>; <a href='https://nces.ed.gov/' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration: none;' target='_blank'>NCES<\/a>; <a href='https://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration: none;' target='_blank'>IPEDS<\/a><\/font><\/div><div style=''><font size='4'>Data download: <a href='https://hifld-dhs-gii.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/4061dcd767c340d4a42fb7a0c6c5d5b4_0?selectedAttributes%5B%5D=STATE&amp;selectedAttributes%5B%5D=POPULATION&amp;chartType=donut&amp;chartColor=%23CB181E&amp;geometry=-79.7%2C42.751%2C-77.614%2C43.052' style='' target='_blank'>Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD): Colleges and Universities<\/a><\/font><\/div><div style=''><div style='line-height: 26.35px;'><font size='4'><font color='#000000' style='line-height: 26.35px;'>For feedback please contact:<\/font><span style='line-height: 26.35px; color: rgb(77, 77, 77);'> <\/span><a href='mailto:ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com' style='color: rgb(33, 117, 155); text-decoration: none; line-height: 26.35px;'>ArcGIScomNationalMaps@esri.com<\/a><br /><\/font><\/div><div><font size='4'><br /><\/font><\/div><\/div><div style=''><font size='4'><i>Thumbnail image courtesy of: <\/i><i><a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration: none;' target='_blank'>Antonio Barrera<\/a><\/i><\/font><\/div><div style=''><i><font size='4'>Symbol source image courtesy of <a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/us/' style='' target='_blank'>Hector<\/a><\/font><\/i><\/div><div style='font-size: 17px;'><span style='font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: white; color: black; font-size: 15pt;'><br /><\/span><\/div><div style='font-size: 17px;'><span style='font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: white; color: black; font-size: 15pt;'>Other Federal User Community federally focused content that may interest you<\/span><br /><\/div><div style='font-size: 17px;'><span style='font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: white; color: black; font-size: 15pt;'><br /><\/span><\/div><div><div style='color: rgb(68, 68, 68); line-height: 16.36px;'><p style='margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.55rem;'><font size='4'><span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir LT W01 35 Light&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(76, 76, 76); line-height: 1.3846;'><span style='font-family: Arial, sans-serif; height: auto; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);'><img alt='USDED - Seal' src='http://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/7d855804b2ec4a4fa99c3935910f917e/data' style='max-width: 100%; height: auto; color: rgb(68, 68, 68); line-height: 18px; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;' /><\/span> <\/span><\/font><a href='http://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/apps/MinimalGallery/index.html?appid=ad0f78f184f24bb9b80ec02b41d0fb3a' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none; font-size: 17px;' target='_blank'><font size='4'>Department of Education<\/font><\/a><font size='4'><span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir LT W01 35 Light&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(76, 76, 76); line-height: 1.3846;'>          <\/span><\/font><span style='font-size: large;'><img alt='AGOL - Open Data logo' src='http://fedmaps.maps.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/46785cfb399344a6af50d4514d6ef0f9/data' style='max-width: 100%; height: auto;' /> <\/span><a href='http://open.fedmaps.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets?q=USDED&amp;sort_by=relevance' style='color: rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line: none; font-size: large;' target='_blank'>Open Data: USDED<\/a><span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir LT W01 35 Light&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: large; color: rgb(76, 76, 76);'> <\/span><br /><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["U.S. Department of Education","Department of Education","USDED","college","university","education","higher learning","professional","school","Post Secondary","specialized institutions","Integrated Post Secondary Education System","National Center for Education Statistics","IPEDS","NCES","places","boundaries","federal"],"snippet":"This feature layer, utilizing data from the U.S. Department of Education (USDED), displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7432,-14.3232],[171.3784,71.3247]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_(USDED)/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":200,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1787396400000},{"id":"2c3c5d1cfdf54f0c89cfb44fe719a3f0","owner":"bwconley","created":1423689658000,"modified":1438625527000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"Parcel Polygon Shapefiles exported from MXD files in ArcGIS 9.3.1 ArcEditor with RPS attribute data joined from the Assessors' 2011 Final Assessment Roll, as of July 1, 2011. Shapefile is for the twelve towns, inclusive of the five villages , as well as the Tuscarora Indian Reservation and a small portion of the Tonawanda Creek Indian Reservation and also the three incorporated cities. Niagara County was created from Genesee County in the year 1808 and is located in the extreme western part of New York State, north of Buffalo adjacent to Lake Ontario on the north and to Canada and the Niagara River on the west. Orleans County is located to the east. Taxable status based on March 1, 2011. Projection is the New York State Plane Coordinate Western Zone NAD83.","tags":["1RF","Colleges and Universities","education","economy","Housing"],"snippet":null,"thumbnail":"thumbnail/colleges.jpg","documentation":null,"extent":[[-79.0548,42.7391],[-78.6916,43.1617]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"County of Niagara Real Property Services, Tax Mapping Division: prepared for Tax purposes only and is NOT to be reproduced for surveying or conveyancing. See also the ESRI License Agreement for Disclaimer of Warranties and Liabilities.","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"CC BY","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://mapservices.ap.buffalo.edu/mapservices/rest/services/EducationalAssets/MapServer/2","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":931,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791561600000,"source":"University at Buffalo, College of Arts and Sciences","licenseConstraintId":"CC-BY-4.0"},{"id":"19c6c7ace8d54767beb361bf9d13606e","owner":"olivam@lattc.edu","created":1792219047000,"modified":1792377825000,"guid":null,"name":"B01","title":"Schools, Colleges and Universities - Los Angeles County (Tile Layer)","type":"Map Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Map Service","Service","WMTS","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p>Public, charter and private schools, colleges and universities in Los Angeles County, with enrollment.<\/p><p><b>Why it matters:<\/b> Schools are prime sites for green schoolyards and stormwater capture, and they show where children are exposed to heat and flooding.<\/p><p>This is the <b>tile layer<\/b>: fast cached map display from county (1:2,311,162, level 8) to neighborhood scale (1:18,056, level 15). Query the data through the paired <a href='https://lattcarch.maps.arcgis.com//home/item.html?id=e0dde01f7a0e4c3db6ab92dd705af791' rel='nofollow ugc'>feature layer<\/a>.<\/p><p><b>Part of:<\/b> LATTC Watershed Demo Study - Community and Environmental Justice (code B01).<\/p><p><b>Processing:<\/b> copied from the source on October 18, 2026, kept to Los Angeles County (layers over 2000 features clipped to the county land boundary), Web Mercator. <\/p><p><b>Source:<\/b> Los Angeles County Enterprise GIS / California Department of Education<\/p><ul><li><a href='https://services.arcgis.com/RmCCgQtiZLDCtblq/arcgis/rest/services/Schools_Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer/0' rel='nofollow ugc'>https://services.arcgis.com/RmCCgQtiZLDCtblq/arcgis/rest/services/Schools_Colleges_and_Universities/FeatureServer/0<\/a><\/li><\/ul>","tags":["LATTC Watershed Demo Study","Community and Environmental Justice","Schools","Colleges and Universities - Los Angeles County","B01","tile layer","watershed","Los Angeles"],"snippet":"Public, charter and private schools, colleges and universities in Los Angeles County, with enrollment. Schools are prime sites for green schoolyards and stormwater capture, and they show where children are exposed to heat and flooding.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-118.85415399869457,33.71348499424721],[-117.69956989860484,34.79273199940601]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"4326","accessInformation":"Los Angeles County Enterprise GIS / California Department of Education","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"Public data from Los Angeles County Enterprise GIS / California Department of Education, republished for the LATTC Watershed Demo Study. Check the source for its terms of use and the most current version.","culture":"","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://tiles.arcgis.com/tiles/VL3y0UFwNNVn5BNL/arcgis/rest/services/Schools_Colleges_and_Universities_Los_Angeles_County_Tile_Package_/MapServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":4,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792396800000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"b10f499b4ab442a1b2494c2c84b1736d","owner":"ParkerMorgan84","created":1481488507000,"modified":1481488533000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"CA Colleges and Universities-Copy","type":"Web Map","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Online","Explorer Web Map","Map","Online Map","Web Map"],"description":"4 year public and private universities, and 2 year public colleges, located in California that have full-time first year undergraduates. <br />Layer for the Interactive Online California Atlas Project, which is sponsored by the California Geographic \r\nAlliance and San Diego State University Department of Geography.<br />2012 \r\ninstitutional characteristics, in-state tuition and undergraduate \r\nenrollment data from National Center for Education Statistics.<br />Median GPA, mascot, image and fun fact acquired from each institution's website where available.<br />","tags":["California Atlas","California Geographic Alliance","CGA","SDSU"],"snippet":"California 4 year public and private universities, and 2 year public colleges","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-135.2666,31.1495],[-102.813,45.9073]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"C. Paloma for the California Geographic Alliance","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<br />","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":null,"proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":107,"scoreCompleteness":98,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1789531200000},{"id":"5c317b362ea141fd9161578c81cedac9","owner":"sara.hedrick@indianaffairs.gov_BIA_Geospatial","created":1755626380000,"modified":1755628032000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Tribal Colleges and Universities Directory","type":"Web Mapping Application","typeKeywords":["Map","Mapping Site","Metadata","Online Map","Web Map"],"description":"<p>Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs) are chartered by their respective tribal governments, including the ten tribes within the largest reservations in the United States. The 35 accredited TCUs operate more than 90 campuses and sites in 15 states\u2014covering most of Indian Country\u2014and serve students from well more than 250 federally recognized Indian tribes. TCUs vary in enrollment (size), focus (liberal arts, sciences, workforce development/training), location (woodlands, desert, frozen tundra, rural, urban), and student population (predominantly American Indian). However, tribal identity is the core of every TCU, and they all share the mission of tribal self-determination and service to their respective communities.<\/p><p>These academically rigorous institutions engage in partnerships with organizations including U.S. Department of the Interior, U.S. Department of Agriculture, U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, the National Science Foundation, National Aeronautics and Space Administration, and universities nationwide to support research and education programs that focus on issues such as climate change, sustainable agriculture, water quality, wildlife population dynamics, and diabetes prevention. Many support distance learning involving state-of-the-art learning environments.<\/p>","tags":["BOGS","Pathways"],"snippet":"Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs) are a category of Minority Serving Institutions in the United States higher education system. They are distinguished as tribal schools because they are chartered by tribal governments and are located on or near American Indian reservations. View this application in a new browser window: https://biamaps.geoplatform.gov/BIE-TCU-Directory/","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-179.934305,12.725041],[-54.074484,72.245342]],"categories":["/Categories/Application","/Categories/Education"],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Bureau of Indian Affairs, Branch of Geospatial Support (BOGS), BIA Pathways Program, Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS) for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database.","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div>No warranty is made by the Bureau of Indian Affairs (BIA) for the use of the data for purposes not intended by the BIA. This GIS Dataset may contain errors. There is no impact on the legal status of the land areas depicted herein and no impact on land ownership. No legal inference can or should be made from the information in this GIS Dataset. The GIS Dataset is prepared strictly for illustrative and reference purposes only and should not be used, and is not intended for legal, survey, engineering or navigation purposes. <\/div><div><br /><\/div><div>These data have been developed from the best available sources. Although efforts have been made to ensure that the data are accurate and reliable, errors and variable conditions originating from source documents and/or the translation of information from source documents to the systems of record continue to exist. Users must be aware of these conditions and bear responsibility for the appropriate use of the information with respect to possible errors, scale, resolution, rectification, positional accuracy, development methodology, time period, environmental and climatic conditions and other circumstances specific to these data. The user is responsible for understanding the accuracy limitations of the data provided herein. The burden for determining fitness for use lies entirely with the user. The user should refer to the accompanying metadata notes for a description of the data and data development procedures. <\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://biamaps.geoplatform.gov/BIE-TCU-Directory/","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":115,"scoreCompleteness":91,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1789794000000,"source":"Bureau of Indian Affairs","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"a6bdd0056adf41d9a28807ef32aa5f37","owner":"planning_cra","created":1738197905000,"modified":1742839877000,"guid":"65437143-E8BD-4094-AA31-5D7E93D75280","name":"College_and_University_Campuses_in_Coachella_Valley.sd","title":"College and University Campuses in Coachella Valley","type":"Service Definition","typeKeywords":[".sd","ArcGIS","Metadata","Service Definition","Online"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>The College and University Campuses feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges point feature classes/shapefiles with a POPULATION value greater than or equal to 500. Also included is a subset of campuses with a POPULATION value under 500 or equal to -999. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Excluded are online institutions and administrative records as well as colleges and universities that do not have a verifiable campus map. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class/shapefile contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the \"Place Keyword\" section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges and Colleges and Universities. Note that attribution is derived from the Colleges and Universities and Supplemental Colleges feature classes/shapefiles. Refer to the metadata of those feature classes/shapefiles for further information regarding attribution. This release includes 21 new records and the removal of 88 records that are no longer applicable based on the sourced datasets.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","tags":["homeland security","homeland defense","emergency response","education","colleges","universities","university","school","training","business","secretarial","professional","computer","cosmetology","barber","education","fine arts","flight","technical","trade","junior college","enrollment","shelters","boundary","campus","institutional characteristics","employment","name","address","type","status","population","facility characteristics"],"snippet":"This feature class/shapefile captures College and University Campuses defined by the Colleges and Universities point feature class/shapefile and Supplemental Colleges point feature class/shapefile for the Homeland Infrastructure Foundation-Level Data (HIFLD) database. (https://hifld-geoplatform.opendata.arcgis.com/)","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-116.972841797454,33.7018094086014],[-116.218777510891,33.9196723780008]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"WGS_1984_Web_Mercator_Auxiliary_Sphere","accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL), National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><p><span>None (Public Use). Users are advised to read the dataset's metadata thoroughly to understand appropriate use and data limitations.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":3,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1744869600000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"322b255253924605b891138ea6fbc6a3","owner":"emontague_IAFC","created":1713375450000,"modified":1743620846000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer"],"description":"<div><span>This feature layer, \nutilizing data from the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES),\n displays colleges and universities in the U.S. and its territories.<\/span><\/div><div><span><br /><\/span><\/div><div>This layer is included in the IN Recruitment Locations Viewer web map (<a href='https://iafc.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=d24f90c7ff3844948cde0fc76f8cfc45' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Overview Page<\/a>), Step 2 of the Indiana Volunteer Firefighter Recruitment Toolkit (<a href='https://iafc.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=54550acbe46b40ff9de1c5e1cc7b010c' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Overview Page<\/a>). For this purpose, the feature layer is filtered to show colleges and universities in Indiana.<\/div>","tags":["college","university","school","education","higher education","U.S. Department of Education","Department of Education","National Center for Education Statistics","NCES","IPEDS","Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System","Institute for Education Sciences","IES","degree","certificate"],"snippet":"Colleges and Universities in the U.S. (Filtered to show locations in Indiana).","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7427739999013,-14.322636000160417],[171.3781290001442,71.32470199994994]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_View/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":722,"scoreCompleteness":81,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1790863200000,"source":"International Association of Fire Chiefs"},{"id":"8a70b7b848644c2c852eb54a162c63f5","owner":"FEMA_MAC","created":1536325272000,"modified":1756398192000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities as defined by the Integrated Post Secondary Education System (IPEDS, http://nces.ed.gov/ipeds/), National Center for Education Statistics (NCES, https://nces.ed.gov/), US Department of Education for the 2016-2017 school year. Included are Doctoral/Research Universities, Masters Colleges and Universities, Baccalaureate Colleges, Associates Colleges, Theological seminaries, Medical Schools and other health care professions, Schools of engineering and technology, business and management, art, music, design, Law schools, Teachers colleges, Tribal colleges, and other specialized institutions. Overall, this data layer covers all 50 states, as well as Puerto Rico and other assorted U.S. territories. This feature class contains all MEDS/MEDS+ as approved by the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team. Complete field and attribute information is available in the \u201dEntities and Attributes\u201d metadata section. Geographical coverage is depicted in the thumbnail above and detailed in the &quot;Place Keyword&quot; section of the metadata. This feature class does not have a relationship class but is related to Supplemental Colleges. Colleges and Universities that are not included in the NCES IPEDS data are added to the Supplemental Colleges feature class when found. This release includes the addition of 345 new records and modifications to the spatial location and/or attribution of 7175 records. The ADDRESS2 field, previously populated with NOT AVAILABLE, has been removed.","tags":["FEMA","Lifeline Safety & Security"],"snippet":"The Colleges and Universities feature class/shapefile is composed of all Post Secondary Education facilities.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1536325315822.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-170.7432,-14.3232],[171.3784,71.3247]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory (ORNL) Geographic Information Science and Technology (GIST) Group, National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) Homeland Security Infrastructure Program (HSIP) Team","classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/ArcGIS/rest/services/Colleges_and_Universities_View/FeatureServer/0","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2808,"scoreCompleteness":75,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792332000000,"source":"FEMA AGOL"},{"id":"b440022f0b904432bf49c93e4177c4ea","owner":"jill.mackin_history","created":1646287434000,"modified":1677704989000,"guid":null,"name":"Tribal_Colleges_and_Universities__TCUs","title":"Tribal Colleges and Universities (TCUs)","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"Digital vector data (points) showing the locations of Indigenous Post-Secondary Educational Institutions in the continental United States and Canada.","tags":["TCUs"],"snippet":"Tribal Colleges, Universities, and other Post-Secondary Indigenous Institutions in the United States and Canada","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-156.679486,31.91738200000003],[-74.60373699999997,71.32470200000006]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Data citation: Oak Ridge National Laboratory, Geographic Information Sciences and Technology Group. Colleges and Universities. 2010. Retrieved Dec 10th, 2021. https://www.sciencebase.gov/catalog/item/4f4e4acee4b07f02db67fb39","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"none","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/9ecg2KpMLcsUv1Oh/arcgis/rest/services/Tribal_Colleges_and_Universities__TCUs/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":4220,"scoreCompleteness":76,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792368000000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"47e6c01881e949bbade84c1a489f04d1","owner":"doctorehazard","created":1489013308000,"modified":1489013338000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Albany-School District Colleges and Universities","type":"Web Map","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Online","Explorer Web Map","Map","Online Map","Web Map"],"description":"<span style='overflow: auto;'><span>The distribution of over 600 of the World's largest urban areas, based on United Nations data.<div><br /><\/div><div>Click\r\n on the ends of the pointers to identify these urban areas, and to get \r\nmore information about them. Zoom in to get a visual representation of \r\ntheir relative sizes.<\/div><\/span><\/span>","tags":["population","city","largest","biggest","cities","demographics"],"snippet":"This map shows the world's largest cities, based on United Nations figures.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-74.1154,42.5255],[-73.3971,42.7795]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"United Nations","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='overflow: auto;'><span><img height='41' src='http://downloads.esri.com/blogs/arcgisonline/esrilogo_new.png' style='border: 0px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: verdana, helvetica, sans-serif;' width='101' /><span style='font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: verdana, helvetica, sans-serif;'>This work is licensed under the Web Services and API Terms of Use.   <\/span><br /><span style='font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: verdana, helvetica, sans-serif;'>                        <\/span><a href='http://links.esri.com/e800-summary' style='color: rgb(33, 117, 155); font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: verdana, helvetica, sans-serif; outline: none !important;' target='_blank'><b><font color='#21759b'>View Summary<\/font><\/b><\/a><span style='font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: verdana, helvetica, sans-serif;'>  |  <\/span><a href='http://www.esri.com/legal/pdfs/e-800-termsofuse.pdf' style='color: rgb(33, 117, 155); font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; orphans: 2; widows: 2; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: verdana, helvetica, sans-serif; outline: none !important;' target='_blank'><b><font color='#21759b'>View Terms of Use<\/font><\/b><\/a><\/span><\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":null,"proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":84,"scoreCompleteness":96,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792116000000},{"id":"b22125a38748488c93f0ebfaba7be6e1","owner":"RobCox_FranklinSt","created":1767384812000,"modified":1776098737000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Fargo Colleges and Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS API for JavaScript","ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"Businesses provides a detailed list of businesses from Data Axle. It includes company name, Standard Industrial Classification (SIC) and North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) industry code and location coordinates for every business in the database.","tags":["Rasmussen"],"snippet":"The 2025 Esri Business Locations Data is extracted from the Data Axle April 2025 data.  Esri's Business Locations data is a comprehensive list of businesses licensed from Data Axle. The business locations dataset contains over 15 million U.S. businesses including name, location and industrial classification code, number of employees, and sales.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-96.8487400002682,46.84643999978229],[-96.7597240002004,46.90636900018161]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Esri; Data Axle","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span>The data are provided by multiple, third party data vendors under license to Esri for inclusion with ArcGIS Business Analyst for use with Esri® software. Each data vendor has its own data licensing policies and may grant varying redistribution rights to end users. Please consult the redistribution rights below for this dataset provided with ArcGIS Business Analyst. As used herein, \"Geodata\" shall mean any digital dataset consisting of geographic data coordinates and associated attributes.<\/span><\/p><p><span>The redistribution rights for this dataset: Redistribution rights are granted by the data vendor for hardcopy renditions or static, electronic map images (for example, .gif, .jpeg) that are plotted, printed, or publicly displayed with proper metadata and source/copyright attribution to the respective data vendor/vendors.<\/span><\/p><p><span>This dataset is licensed and requires a license file for access.<\/span><\/p><p><span>The terms and conditions below apply to all the datasets provided with ArcGIS Business Analyst.<\/span><\/p><p><span>Proprietary Rights and Copyright: Licensee acknowledges that the Data and Related Materials contain proprietary and confidential property of Esri and its licensor(s). The Data and Related Materials are owned by Esri and its licensor(s) and are protected by United States copyright laws and applicable international copyright treaties and/or conventions.<\/span><\/p><p><span>Limited Warranty and Disclaimer: Esri warrants that the media upon which the Data and Related Materials are provided will be free from defects in materials and workmanship under normal use and service for a period of ninety (90) days from the date of receipt.<\/span><\/p><p><span>THE DATA AND RELATED MATERIALS ARE EXCLUDED FROM THE LIMITED WARRANTY, AND THE LICENSEE EXPRESSLY ACKNOWLEDGES THAT THE DATA CONTAINS SOME NONCONFORMITIES, DEFECTS, OR ERRORS. Esri DOES NOT WARRANT THAT THE DATA WILL MEET LICENSEE'S NEEDS OR EXPECTATIONS; THAT THE USE OF THE DATA WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED; OR THAT ALL NONCONFORMITIES, DEFECTS, OR ERRORS CAN OR WILL BE CORRECTED. Esri IS NOT INVITING RELIANCE ON THIS DATA, AND THE LICENSEE SHOULD ALWAYS VERIFY ACTUAL DATA.<\/span><\/p><p><span>EXCEPT FOR THE LIMITED WARRANTY SET FORTH ABOVE, THE DATA AND RELATED MATERIALS CONTAINED THEREIN ARE PROVIDED \"AS-IS,\" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.<\/span><\/p><p><span>HIGH RISK ACTIVITIES:<\/span><span>(A) THE DATA AND RELATED MATERIALS ARE NOT FAULT-TOLERANT AND ARE NOT DESIGNED, MANUFACTURED, OR INTENDED FOR USE OR RESALE FOR INSURANCE UNDERWRITING OR WITH CRITICAL HEALTH AND SAFETY OR ONLINE CONTROL EQUIPMENT IN HAZARDOUS ENVIRONMENTS THAT REQUIRE FAIL-SAFE PERFORMANCE, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE OPERATION OF NUCLEAR FACILITIES, NAVIGATION OR GUIDANCE (I.E., AIRCRAFT, NAUTICAL VEHICLE, ETC.), OR COMMUNICATION SYSTEMS, AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL, EMERGENCY RESPONSE, TERRORISM PREVENTION OR RESPONSE, LIFE SUPPORT, OR WEAPONS SYSTEMS (\"HIGH RISK ACTIVITIES\"). Esri SPECIFICALLY DISCLAIMS ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTY OF FITNESS FOR HIGH RISK ACTIVITIES.<\/span><span>(B) TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, LICENSEE AGREES TO INDEMNIFY, DEFEND, AND HOLD Esri, ITS OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AGENTS, SUBCONTRACTORS, LICENSORS, SUCCESSORS, AN