nir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;'>, with Spokane County highlighted. T<\/span><span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;'>his app was last updated on 07/27/2018<\/span>","tags":["Washington"],"snippet":"Map of Washington State boundaries and counties, with Spokane County highlighted. Valid form 07/2018.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-126.2149,45.3167],[-115.2835,49.2421]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Federal Emergency Management Agency; Spokane County; Washington State","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<span style='font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;'>Data in this product is all open source and does not contain any Personally Identifiable Information (PII).<\/span>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":null,"proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":117,"scoreCompleteness":81,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792234800000,"source":"California State University San Marcos GIS Lab","licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"4ce1a85da9d3469eacb7c481d5d503a4","owner":"WyomingGeoHub","created":1503007080000,"modified":1564688550000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Census - College And Universities","type":"Map Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Map Service","Metadata","Service"],"description":"The TIGER/Line shapefiles and related database files (.dbf) are an extract of selected geographic and cartographic information from the U.S. Census Bureau's Master Address File / Topologically Integrated Geographic Encoding and Referencing (MAF/TIGER) Database (MTDB). The MTDB represents a seamless national file with no overlaps or gaps between parts, however, each TIGER/Line shapefile is designed to stand alone as an independent data set, or they can be combined to cover the entire nation. ZIP Code Tabulation Areas (ZCTAs) are approximate area representations of U.S. Postal Service (USPS) ZIP Code service areas that the Census Bureau creates to present statistical data for each decennial census. The Census Bureau delineates ZCTA boundaries for the United States, Puerto Rico, American Samoa, Guam, the Commonwealth of the Northern Mariana Islands, and the U.S. Virgin Islands once each decade following the decennial census. Data users should not use ZCTAs to identify the official USPS ZIP Code for mail delivery. The USPS makes periodic changes to ZIP Codes to support more efficient mail delivery. The Census Bureau uses tabulation blocks as the basis for defining each ZCTA. Tabulation blocks are assigned to a ZCTA based on the most frequently occurring ZIP Code for the addresses contained within that block. The most frequently occurring ZIP Code also becomes the five-digit numeric code of the ZCTA. These codes may contain leading zeros. Blocks that do not contain addresses but are surrounded by a single ZCTA (enclaves) are assigned to the surrounding ZCTA. Because the Census Bureau only uses the most frequently occurring ZIP Code to assign blocks, a ZCTA may not exist for every USPS ZIP Code. Some ZIP Codes may not have a matching ZCTA because too few addresses were associated with the specific ZIP Code or the ZIP Code was not the most frequently occurring ZIP Code within any of the blocks where it exists. The ZCTA boundaries in this release are those delineated following the 2010 Census.","tags":["US Census","Wyoming","Colleges","Universities","School","Education","Boundaries","Administrative and Political Boundaries","Business","Business and Economy","Economy","Facilities","Facilities and Structures","Society","Cultural","Demographic"],"snippet":null,"thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG","documentation":null,"extent":[[-113,39],[-100,46]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"english (united states)","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.wygisc.org/HostGIS/rest/services/GeoHub/CensusCollegesUniversities/MapServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2599,"scoreCompleteness":66,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1792317600000},{"id":"54571d3076524175ac521b5089de8a7f","owner":"pablogreene143","created":1693288427000,"modified":1693289199000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"UCGIS Membership of TRELIS Participants Compared to Black Enrolment in Colleges and Universities","type":"Web Mapping Application","typeKeywords":["JavaScript","Map","Mapping Site","Online Map","Web Map"],"description":"The map indicates UCGIS institutions and the institutions that have participated in the TRELIS program. The amount of overlap between the data sets indicate the success the UCGIS have had in having non members participate in the TRELIS program.In the background there is a heat map indicating institutions with high black enrollment. This map may be used to determine where to expand the UCGIS to make a more equitable membership pool.","tags":["GIS","UCGIS","demographics","College demographics","TRELIS"],"snippet":"This map indicates whether TRELIS participants where already UCGIS members and comparing that data to college demograpgics.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1693289198872.png","documentation":null,"extent":[],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":"No terms. Free to use. ","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://www.arcgis.com/apps/View/index.html?appid=54571d3076524175ac521b5089de8a7f","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":79,"scoreCompleteness":98,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1790182800000},{"id":"81fbf77c5ef44628a13ac55dbfe28de2","owner":"KelleyMaps","created":1493409056000,"modified":1499820885000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges and Universities: USA and Canada","type":"Web Map","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Online","Collector","Data Editing","Explorer Web Map","Map","Online Map","Web Map"],"description":"<p style='box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(33, 33, 33); font-family: truenolight, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);'>The College Sleep Environmental Scan for residential colleges and universities addresses how institutional policy, programming, and structures contribute to or impede healthy sleep. While environmental scans exist for a variety of campus issues including alcohol safety, environmental stewardship, and openness to GLBT students, there are no such scans available for assessing how campus environmental factors impact students' sleep. The College Sleep Environmental Scan provides important normative and formative data for universities and colleges to consider in identifying and implementing strategies for institution-wide changes to improve poor sleep. Poor sleep is one of the top five impediments to academic success.<\/p>","tags":["College","Universities"],"snippet":"The mission of the Center for College Sleep is to better understand and improve college sleep by providing rigorous research, educational outreach, and innovative programming. ","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-180,-6.9874],[19.621,71.1963]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":null,"classification":null,"licenseInfo":null,"culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":null,"proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":414,"scoreCompleteness":75,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791687600000},{"id":"b9a05a6d53ac48778383ec9d18d5b816","owner":"CCGIS2025","created":1553542693000,"modified":1737471586000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Colleges And Universities","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"Cumberland County colleges and universities.","tags":["Community Services","colleges","universities"],"snippet":"Cumberland County colleges and universities.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-78.93213405653606,35.06493489775123],[-78.86136997610534,35.13845354692754]],"categories":["/Categories/Society"],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"CCGIS","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div>Cumberland County GIS (CCGIS) makes no guarantee as to the content, accuracy, precision or completeness of any information and services provided. While Cumberland County aims to maintain up-to-date and accurate information, no guarantee is provided that the data, maps, applications, and services are current. Changes in geographic features, boundaries, infrastructure, and other features and factors may not be reflected immediately. Regular maintenance and updates are conducted, but data offered is provided without warranty. The user should consult public primary information sources, such as recorded deeds and plats, to verify the accuracy of the data provided. Some data, maps, applications, and services may include data provided by third parties, and links to external websites may be provided for additional information. Cumberland County is not responsible for the accuracy, reliability, or timeliness of third-party data or external content. Any data from third-party sources should be independently verified before being used.  The user of this website understands and accepts that the use of any information is strictly voluntary and at the user\u2019s sole risk. The user is responsible for understanding the limitations, conditions, and appropriate use of GIS data. The data, maps, applications, and services should not be interpreted as exact representations of geographic or property boundaries, public or private infrastructure, or other features. The user should cross-reference data and consult primary sources to verify data accuracy, especially when making legal, property, or financial decisions. Spatial data is subject to distortions due to scale, resolution, and projection systems. Cumberland County cadastral data are a presentation of recorded plats and surveys for use within the CCGIS for purposes of data access and analysis. These and other data do not replace or modify land surveys, deeds, and/or other legal instruments defining land ownership or use. This site is a public service to the citizens of Cumberland County and to the Internet Community. Information provided on the maps, applications and services is not intended to replace any official source and should not be considered authoritative to be used for decision-making. The records are made available for informational purposes only, gathered from various sources, some of which are updated frequently. This information sho